window.BALM_SEARCH=[{"t":"Getting started","p":"Getting started","u":"index.html","x":"Balm is an Online Store 2.0 theme for Shopify: every page is built from sections and blocks that you add, remove and reorder in the theme editor, without code. This guide takes you from installation to a store ready to publish."},{"t":"Install Balm from the Theme Store","p":"Getting started","u":"index.html#install","x":"Open the Balm page on the Shopify Theme Store while logged in to your store. Select View demo store to browse Balm with its content before you install it. Select Try theme to add a trial copy to your theme library, or buy the theme straight away. A trial lets you customize everything; you pay when you publish. In your admin, go to Online Store, Themes . Balm is in your theme library. Select Customize to open the theme editor. When the store is ready, open the theme's ... menu in the theme library and choose Publish . Balm needs no app to work. Apps that offer app blocks, such as reviews, subscriptions or bundles, plug into the product page and into most sections."},{"t":"Updating Balm","p":"Getting started / Install Balm from the Theme Store","u":"index.html#updates","x":"When a new version is released, your theme library shows an update notice. Shopify adds the new version to your library as a separate copy that keeps your theme editor settings and content, so you can review it before publishing. Changes made directly in the theme code are not carried over: see Custom code . What changed in each version is listed in the Changelog ."},{"t":"The Balm preset","p":"Getting started","u":"index.html#preset","x":"A preset is a starting style: color schemes, font pairing, corner radii, glass recipe and typography recipes. Balm comes with one preset, also named Balm, and your store starts from it. Look. Clean and neutral: a white scheme, a near black scheme and two violet schemes (a pale lavender and a deep violet), sentence case headings and buttons, a white frosted glass. A calm base that lets product photography lead. Fonts. Outfit 400 for headings, Inter for body text, on one fluid type scale. Layout. Pages in Full width with margins, lined up with the header, and small buttons. Corners. Softly rounded: buttons 12 px, cards 20 px. Every value of the preset is a starting point. Change the colors, fonts, corners, glass and typography in Theme settings ; your sections, blocks and content stay as they are."},{"t":"How the theme editor is organized","p":"Getting started","u":"index.html#editor","x":"Header group : the Announcement bar and the Header, shared by every page. Template : the sections of the page you are editing. Switch page type with the menu at the top of the editor (Home page, Products, Collections and so on). Footer group : the Footer, shared by every page. Theme settings (the gear icon): colors, fonts and storewide features. See Theme settings . Most sizes and spacings have two settings, one ending in (desktop) and one ending in (mobile) , so you can tune phones without touching large screens. Spacings switch from one value to the other at 768 px wide. Text sizes are fluid: the mobile value applies on a phone 390 px wide, the desktop value from 1440 px, and the size moves smoothly in between (see Typography ). Use the device switch at the top of the editor to preview both."},{"t":"First setup, step by step","p":"Getting started","u":"index.html#first-setup","x":"Logo and menu. Open the Header section. Set Logo type and upload your Logo image , then pick your main menu under Menu . Menus themselves are edited in your admin, under Content, Menus (Online Store, Navigation on older admins). The header is transparent over the first section by default and picks its colors from what lies under it: upload a white logo in Logo for dark backgrounds so it reads over dark images (see Automatic header colors ). Countries and languages. The header shows a globe with the country and language selectors as soon as there is a choice to make: two countries or regions in Settings, Markets , or two published languages in Settings, Languages . Until then it shows nothing. Country and language selectors in the Header picks which ones appear (Both by default). See Country and language selectors . Colors. In Theme settings, Colors , adjust the four color schemes of the Balm preset to your brand. Every section picks one of them. Fonts, sizes and corners. Set the Heading font and Body font in Typography . To make every heading or every text of the store larger or smaller at once, move Heading scale or Body scale there rather than each section's sizes. Set the corner"},{"t":"Templates included","p":"Getting started","u":"index.html#templates","x":"Home page, product, collection, list of collections, search, cart, blog, blog post, page, 404, password and gift card, a second product template, product.immersive (each product's own gradient under the header, see Extend the gradient under the header ), a second collection template, collection.colorful (an Aurora gradient that runs under the header, with the column selector on), plus five page templates: page.about (About), page.contact (Contact), page.faq (FAQ), page.find-us (Store locator) and page.products (Products). All of them are built from sections, so you can reshape any of them in the editor."},{"t":"Need help?","p":"Getting started","u":"index.html#help","x":"Search this documentation with the box at the top of the page, read the FAQ , or contact Balm support ."},{"t":"Theme settings","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html","x":"Theme settings apply to the whole store. Open them in the theme editor with the Theme settings icon (the gear) in the left bar. The groups below follow the order of the editor, and every label is written exactly as the editor shows it. The Default column gives the theme's built in value; the Balm preset, which your store starts from, replaces the colors, fonts, corners, glass and typography values with its own."},{"t":"Setting groups","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#groups","x":"Colors Typography Layout Corner style Buttons Product cards Product badges Pre-order Quick view Cart Gift wrapping Back to top Age verifier Glass effect Backgrounds Carousels Loader Favicon Social media Social media sharing Breadcrumbs Search Filters Search engines"},{"t":"Colors","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-colors","x":"Balm organizes its colors in color schemes . A scheme is a set of seven colors designed to work together, and every section, popup and drawer picks one scheme with its own Color scheme setting. Edit a scheme here and every place that uses it follows. The Balm preset ships two schemes. Scheme 1 is the main one, white; Scheme 2 is its contrasting partner, near black. Add as many schemes as you need with Add scheme . Background : the section background. Background gradient is optional and replaces it where set. Text : body text, headings and icons. Button / accent and Button label : the fill and the text of primary buttons. Secondary background : the second surface of the scheme, used by cards, drawers, panels, inputs and secondary buttons. Balm derives a raised tone and a hairline from it, so dark schemes keep visible layers. Accent (links / highlights) : links and highlighted details. Keep the text and button colors readable on their background: aim for a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 for body text. Glass surfaces measure their own contrast and switch the label to black or white when needed, but plain surfaces use exactly the colors you set.","l":"Accent (links / highlights) | Background | Background gradient | Button / accent | Button label | Secondary background | Text"},{"t":"Typography","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-typography","x":"Two fonts drive the whole theme: the Heading font for headings and titles, and the Body font for paragraphs, forms and everything else. Both come from the Shopify font library, so they are served by Shopify and free to use on your store. The Balm preset pairs Outfit 400 for headings with Inter for body text. Type sizes. Balm sets its text on one fluid scale. Every size has a mobile value, reached on a screen 390 px wide, and a desktop value, reached at 1440 px. In between, the size grows in a straight line; outside that range, it holds at the nearer value. On the scale, the product title runs from 32 to 44 px, section headings from 26 to 36 px, card titles from 15 to 17 px, body text from 15 to 16 px and small text from 12 to 13 px, each level with its own line height and letter spacing. The text size settings of sections and blocks follow the same rule: the value of a setting ending in (mobile) applies at 390 px, the one ending in (desktop) at 1440 px, and the size moves smoothly between them. Their defaults sit on the scale, so a section you add matches the rest of the page. The announcement bar and the mega menu are the exceptions: they switch from one value to the other at the ","l":"Body font | Body scale | Heading case | Heading font | Heading scale | Heading style | Heading weight | Label case | Label letter spacing | Label style"},{"t":"Layout","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-layout","x":"Page width sets how wide the content of the product, collection and search pages can grow, together with the Featured collection, Product recommendations and Recently viewed sections. Standard , the default: 1400 px at most, centered. Wide : 1600 px at most. Full width with margins : the whole screen, less the side margins of the header. The page content, the breadcrumbs and the footer then line up with the logo and the icons of the header, a floating header included. Product card images are served at the size the chosen width draws them, so cards stay sharp on a wider page. The other sections set their own width with their Section width setting, whose Page width option stops at the width chosen here: see Section width .","l":"Page width"},{"t":"Corner style","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-corner-style","x":"Four sliders set the maximum corner radius of the whole theme: Buttons and pills , Cards and panels , Form fields and Images and media . Each value is a ceiling: elements designed with smaller corners keep them, and 0 gives square corners everywhere. Section settings that carry their own radius, such as the floating header or the cart drawer, are capped by these values too. The Balm preset sets buttons and form fields to 12 px, cards and media to 20 px.","l":"Buttons and pills | Cards and panels | Form fields | Images and media"},{"t":"Buttons","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-buttons","x":"One recipe for every button of the theme, primary and secondary. Size (Small, Medium by default, or Large) sets the height, the padding and the text size on desktop and on mobile, one step down or up the type scale from Medium. A Small button keeps a tap area of 44 px around it. Border width (1 or 2 px) applies to outline buttons, and Font weight (Regular, Medium or Semibold) to every label. The case, letter spacing and slant of the labels are set in Typography , the corners in Corner style . A few buttons can step out of the shared size: the Buy buttons block of the product page ( Button size ), the quick add button of the cards ( Size in Product cards ) and the button of a Products showcase spotlight. Each offers Follow buttons , which keeps this setting.","l":"Border width | Font weight | Size"},{"t":"Product cards","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-product-cards","x":"One look for the product cards of the Collection, Search, Featured collection, Product recommendations, Recently viewed and Lookbook sections, set once here. Sizes. The title and price sizes, on desktop and on mobile. The defaults sit on the type scale : titles 17 px on desktop and 15 px on mobile, prices 16 and 14 px, with the compare-at price at 85% of the price. Heading scale applies to the titles, Body scale to the prices. The cards of the 404 page follow them too; the Complementary products block of the product page keeps its own title size. Image. Hover effect decides what a mouse does to the picture. With Second image on hover turned on in the section, Fade crossfades the product's two images and Swap changes them at once. Zoom enlarges the image, and crossfades to the second one when it is on. Quick add button. The style of the card button (Add to cart, Choose options, Shop now): Solid, Outline, Text link, Glass or Icon only (a bag icon), Auto or Full width, below the product details or on the image (shown on hover on desktop, always on touch screens), and the button colors of the color scheme or your own. Its size follows Buttons unless you pick one here. Where the button "},{"t":"Text behind cutouts on the cards","p":"Theme settings / Product cards","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-product-cards-cutouts","x":"The product's title, or its custom.tagline metafield, can stand as a large decorative text behind the picture of each card of a collection grid, seen through the transparent areas of PNG and WebP images. JPG images never get it. The Collection section decides where it shows, with Text behind cutouts , Show on desktop and Show on mobile ; this group sets its look for every card at once: Text , Font , Font weight , Text case , Letter spacing , Line height , Lines , the vertical and horizontal position per device, the Text color (the scheme text, the product's custom.background_color_end metafield or a custom color), Text opacity (15% by default) and Text style , Solid or Outline with its thickness. The text is hidden from screen readers. The product page has its own version of it: see Text behind cutout images . Image Quick add button Text behind cutouts","l":"Background color | Border color | Colors | Custom color | Font | Font weight | Horizontal position (desktop) | Horizontal position (mobile) | Hover effect | Letter spacing | Line height | Lines | Outline thickness | Position | Price size (desktop) | Price size (mobile) | Product title size (desktop) | Product title size (mobile) | Size | Style | Text | Text and icon color | Text case | Text color | Text opacity | Text style | Vertical position (desktop) | Vertical position (mobile) | Width"},{"t":"Product badges","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-product-badges","x":"Four badges can sit on the product cards, in quick view, in Compare products and on the product page. Sale shows automatically when the compare-at price is above the price, Sold out when the product can no longer be bought. New is off by default: set New badge to Product tag and name the tag, or to Created in the last X days and set the number of days. Custom prints the product's custom.badge_label metafield, read directly. This group sets their position, shape and colors once for the whole store. A product can give its Custom badge its own colors through two optional Color metafields, custom.badge_color (background) and custom.badge_text_color (text). Left empty, the badge uses Custom background and Custom text from this group. With a background and no text color, the text turns dark or light by itself, at a contrast of at least 4.5:1. See Give one product its own badge colors . On the product page, turn on Badges on media in the Product section, or add a Badge block. Every section that shows product cards has its own Badges setting (All, Automatic only, Custom only or None) to keep some of them, or none, in that section: see Choose the badges of each section . See Product badges ","l":"Custom background | Custom text | New background | New badge | New text | Number of days (X) | Position | Sale background | Sale badge text | Sale text | Shape | Sold out background | Sold out text | Tag"},{"t":"Pre-order","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-pre-order","x":"Pre-order turns itself on for a variant whose quantity is tracked, whose stock is at 0 and that has Continue selling when out of stock checked. The add to cart button, the sticky add to cart bar and the quick add button then read Pre-order , or the label you type here. See Pre-order .","l":"Button label"},{"t":"Quick view","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-quick-view","x":"Quick view opens a product in a modal from its card, so shoppers can pick a variant and add to cart without leaving the page. This group sets what the modal shows and how it looks. You turn it on per section, with the Quick view setting of the Collection, Featured collection, Search, Recently viewed and Lookbook sections. See Quick view . Button on cards Content Card","l":"Background color | Card opacity | Card style | Color scheme | Colors | Description length | Icon | Icon and label color | Preload on hover | Shape | Short description metafield | Show link to the product page | Show pickup availability | Show rating | Show short description | Show vendor | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile)"},{"t":"Cart","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-cart","x":"The whole cart is set up here, once: the drawer, the notification and the cart page share these settings, so the Cart drawer section has none of its own. Cart type : Drawer (the default) slides a panel in after each add, Page opens the cart page, Notification confirms the add with the line just added, View cart and Check out. Drawer and notification : Style Solid (the color scheme's background) or Glass (the Glass effect over the whole drawer, top to bottom). Floating drawer , on by default, detaches the drawer and the notification from the screen edges by the margins you set for desktop and mobile, with the corners of Corner style . Panel width, paddings, heading and title sizes, thumbnail size and Line density (Comfortable, or Compact for a smaller thumbnail and tighter lines, in the drawer and on the cart page) follow. Colors : Text colors on Color scheme keeps the scheme's text; on Auto, the cart reads its real background, glass included, and keeps the scheme text when it reaches 4.5:1, otherwise white or black. Free shipping bar : progress toward the Free shipping threshold you type, in your store currency and converted for visitors who shop in another one. Nothing shows while","l":"Ask about lines in this order | Bar background | Bar fill | Bar height | Bar style | Button label | Button link | Card size | Cart type | Color scheme | Corner radius | Floating drawer | Free shipping threshold | Glass | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Horizontal padding (desktop) | Horizontal padding (mobile) | Layout | Line density | Margin from the screen edges (desktop) | Margin from the screen edges (mobile) | Measure progress on | Message | Message before the threshold | Message once reached | Number of products | Order note label | Order note placeholder | Panel width (desktop) | Position | Product title size | Products | Products come from | Products heading | Promotion note text | Recommendation type | Row icon | Shipping notice | Show a promotion note on each line | Show accelerated checkout buttons in the drawer | Show accelerated checkout buttons on the cart page | Show payment icons | Show price | Show products | Show quick add | Show recommendations | Show shipping notice | Show the discount code field | Show the free shipping bar | Show the order note | Show the taxes and shipping note | Show the total savings | Style | Text colors | Thumbnail size"},{"t":"Gift wrapping","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-gift-wrapping","x":"Adds a gift wrapping checkbox, and an optional gift message, to the cart drawer and the cart page. The wrapping is a real product you create in your admin, so its price, taxes and stock work like any other product. See Gift wrapping for the setup. Gift message Where to show it","l":"Checkbox label | Help text | Message label | Message maximum length (characters) | Offer a gift message | Offer gift wrapping | Show help text | Show in the cart drawer | Show on the cart page | Wrapping product"},{"t":"Back to top","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-back-to-top","x":"A round button in a bottom corner that scrolls back to the top of the page. It appears after the visitor has scrolled the distance set in Show after scrolling , can be turned on for desktop and mobile separately, lifts above the sticky add to cart bar and steps aside from the hero video controls. Visitors who ask their device for reduced motion get an instant jump instead of a smooth scroll.","l":"Background color | Icon color | Position | Show a back to top button | Show after scrolling | Show on desktop | Show on mobile | Style"},{"t":"Age verifier","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-age-verifier","x":"A modal that asks visitors to confirm their age before they browse the store, for brands that sell alcohol, tobacco or other age restricted products. The answer is remembered in the visitor's browser for the number of days you choose. See Age verifier . Content When the visitor declines Look","l":"Action | Background image | Card opacity | Card style | Color scheme | Confirm button | Decline button | Enable the age verifier | Heading | Link | Message | Minimum age | Preview in the theme editor | Remember the answer for | Text"},{"t":"Glass effect","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-glass-effect","x":"One frosted glass recipe shared by every glass surface of the theme: the glass header and mega menu, the announcement bar in Glass style, glass buttons, the popups and the cart drawer when they use a glass card. Set the Tint , Fill opacity , Blur and Border opacity once and every surface moves together. Glass on phones decides what happens on screens under 768 px wide: Frosted keeps the blur, Near opaque swaps it for an almost solid fill that is lighter to scroll on older phones. Browsers without backdrop blur and visitors who ask for reduced transparency always get the near opaque fill. Glass elements is a second, lighter recipe for the small pieces set to Glass inside the sections: cards, FAQ questions, form fields, buttons and the round controls that sit over a picture (carousel arrows, Lookbook hotspots, the media controls of the product gallery, the video controls of the Hero). Element fill opacity , Element blur and Element border opacity set it; the tint is the one above. These elements turn nearly solid for visitors who ask for less transparency. See Glass . Glass elements","l":"Blur | Border opacity | Element blur | Element border opacity | Element fill opacity | Fill opacity | Glass on phones | Tint"},{"t":"Backgrounds","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-backgrounds","x":"The section backgrounds set to Gradient (two colors) can take three styles, chosen in each section with Gradient style : Linear, Radial glow (a halo of the lighter color, placed and sized by the halo settings) or Aurora (soft fields of the two colors). Animate auroras slowly , off by default, sets every Aurora of the store in a very slow movement. It stays still for visitors whose device asks for reduced motion. See Section background .","l":"Animate auroras slowly"},{"t":"Carousels","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-carousels","x":"One look for the arrows and the dots of every carousel: the product gallery, Product recommendations, Testimonials, Key ingredients and the other sliders of the theme. Arrow style : Solid, Outline, Glass (the Glass elements recipe, with a halo that keeps the arrow readable over a light or a dark photo) or Icon only. Arrow shape (Square, Rounded, Circle), Arrow size on desktop and on mobile, and Arrow icon (Arrow or Chevron). Arrow colors : Auto takes the colors of the section around the carousel, readable on its real background; Custom uses Arrow background and Arrow icon color . Dots style : Dots or Bars. Where the arrows sit (on the sides, on hover, below, with dots, or none) is set in each section. Carousels move one card at a time, follow a mouse drag and the keyboard, and stay still for visitors who ask for reduced motion.","l":"Arrow background | Arrow colors | Arrow icon | Arrow icon color | Arrow shape | Arrow size (desktop) | Arrow size (mobile) | Arrow style | Dots style"},{"t":"Loader","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-loader","x":"The Page loader : an optional loading screen shown while pages open, with your logo, a progress bar or a spinner, and an exit animation. It is the theme's only loader, and it covers everything on the page, the header and the announcement bar included. See Page loader . The progress bar has three settings of its own, shown with the Logo and progress bar and Progress bar only layouts: Bar ends (Square, or Rounded, the default, which rounds the track and the fill), Bar thickness (1 to 6 px, 2 by default) and Bar animation (None, Smooth by default, or Shimmer). Preview versions of Balm had a second loader here: a loading indicator drawn on the hero while its video loaded, with seven settings (Style, Loader image, Animation, Size (desktop), Size (mobile), Color and Custom color). It has been removed with those settings. The hero now shows its cover image while its video loads, sharp or blurred, as set by While the video loads in the Hero section. Page loader","l":"Background | Bar animation | Bar ends | Bar thickness | Color scheme | Exit animation | Exit duration | Glass opacity | Layout | Logo image | Logo width (desktop) | Logo width (mobile) | Maximum display time | Minimum display time | Page loader | Page transitions | Preview in the theme editor"},{"t":"Favicon","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-favicon","x":"The small icon shown in browser tabs and bookmarks. Upload a square image of at least 32 by 32 pixels; a PNG with a transparent background works best.","l":"Favicon"},{"t":"Social media","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-social-media","x":"The addresses of your profiles, typed once: Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, X, YouTube, Pinterest, Snapchat, Threads, Tumblr, Vimeo and LinkedIn. Enter the full URL of each profile, for example https://www.instagram.com/yourbrand . Only the networks with a URL show, each with its icon, in the order of this list. A link opens in a new tab and is named for screen readers after your store, such as Balm on Instagram . The icons appear in three places: the Social media links block of the footer, the Social media links section, and the header on desktop when Show social media icons is checked in the Header section. See Social media .","l":"Facebook | Instagram | LinkedIn | Pinterest | Snapchat | Threads | TikTok | Tumblr | Vimeo | X | YouTube"},{"t":"Social media sharing","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-social-media-sharing","x":"Controls how your pages look when someone shares a link on social media or in a messaging app. Product, collection and blog post pages use their own featured image. The Fallback share image covers every other page (1200 x 630 pixels is the recommended size), and the X (Twitter) account is shown as the source of shared cards. The links to your own profiles are in Social media .","l":"Fallback share image | X (Twitter) account"},{"t":"Breadcrumbs","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-breadcrumbs","x":"A trail of links back to the home page, shown on product, collection and blog post pages. Position, separator and alignment are set here for the whole store. The Product, Collection and Article sections each have a Breadcrumbs on this page setting that shows or hides the trail on that page type only. Show the collection , on by default, adds a collection to the trail of a product page, and to the breadcrumb data search engines read: the collection the visitor came through, otherwise the collection set in the product's custom.primary_collection metafield, otherwise its first collection. See Metafields, Primary collection .","l":"Alignment | Position | Separator | Show breadcrumbs | Show the collection"},{"t":"Search","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-search","x":"Search scope decides what the storefront searches, both in the header suggestions and on the results page. Products only keeps the results page to product cards, which is also what the search filters need. Products, articles and pages adds your blog posts and pages to the results.","l":"Search scope"},{"t":"Filters","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-filters","x":"Filter drawer style sets the look of the filter drawer: the panel opened by the Filter and sort button on phones, and by the Filters button when the Collection or Search section uses the Drawer filter layout. Solid uses the section's color scheme, Glass the Glass effect , like the cart drawer. The drawer opens over the announcement bar and the header, full height, with the filters in accordions, Sort by on phones, and Clear all and Apply fixed at the bottom. The filters themselves come from Shopify's Search & Discovery app.","l":"Filter drawer style"},{"t":"Search engines","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-search-engines","x":"Shopify already tells search engines to treat a filtered or sorted collection URL as the plain collection URL. Internal search results pages are not covered by default, and they rarely deserve a place in Google. This setting adds a noindex instruction to them, and optionally to filtered collections too.","l":"Keep out of search results"},{"t":"Sections","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html","x":"Every section Balm offers, with where it can be used, what it does, a typical use and its full list of settings. Add a section from the theme editor with Add section; drag it to reorder it. Settings tables are folded: open one to see every label, its values and its default."},{"t":"All sections","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#all-sections","x":"Header and footer Announcement bar Header Footer Hero and storytelling Hero Slideshow Products showcase Featured set Image Image with text Rich text Scroll-revealed text Bento Video Marquee Before and after Products and collections Featured product Featured collection Collection list Routine Lookbook Compare products Recently viewed Trust and engagement Key ingredients Key figures Multicolumn Testimonials Logo list Countdown Newsletter Newsletter popup Social media links FAQ About page Brand story hero Comparison panels Checklist banner Gallery banner Contact and stores Contact Store locator Layout, code and apps Divider Custom Liquid Apps Template sections Product Product recommendations Sticky add to cart Collection Search Collections list Cart Cart drawer Blog Article Page 404 page Password page Gift card Blocks used inside sections Theme blocks Mega menu blocks"},{"t":"Settings most sections share","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#shared-settings","x":"A handful of settings come back in almost every section. They work the same way everywhere, so they are explained once here."},{"t":"Color scheme","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#color-scheme","x":"Picks one of the schemes defined in Theme settings, Colors . The scheme paints the section background, its text and its buttons."},{"t":"Section background","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#section-background","x":"Most sections can paint their own background on top of the color scheme. Background mode offers five choices, and the settings of the mode you pick appear right below it: None (use the color scheme) : the default. The scheme background shows, like everywhere else. Solid color : one Background color . Gradient (two colors) : Gradient start , Gradient end and Gradient angle . Image : a Background image with an optional Overlay color and Overlay opacity to keep text readable. Radial halo : a Halo color glowing from one corner over a Base color , with Halo position , Halo size (desktop) , Halo size (mobile) and Halo solid area . A gradient takes a Gradient style : Linear, Radial glow (a halo of the lighter color, placed and sized by the halo settings) or Aurora (soft fields of the two colors, which Theme settings, Backgrounds can set in slow motion). An image takes an optional Background image (mobile) , used under 768 px, and each picture shows at its focal point. Grain lays a light texture over any mode; 0 turns it off. The colors and the image can be connected to shop metafields , so one value restyles every section at once. The Fallback background color is used when a connected met"},{"t":"Spacing, desktop and mobile","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#spacing","x":"Sizes and spacings come in pairs: a label ending in (desktop) applies from 768 px wide, one ending in (mobile) applies below. Top and bottom padding set the space inside the section, above and below its content. Text sizes are the exception: they are fluid. The (mobile) value applies on a screen 390 px wide, the (desktop) value from 1440 px, and the size moves smoothly in between, then Heading scale or Body scale multiplies it. See Theme settings, Typography . The announcement bar and the mega menu switch their text sizes at 1200 px instead, and decorative texts, such as the text behind cutouts of the Product section, keep a desktop and a mobile size off the scale."},{"t":"Section width","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#section-width","x":"Almost every section has a Section width setting, right after its color scheme. It sets how far the section's background, image or card reaches: Full width : from one edge of the screen to the other. Pictures and videos (Image, Image with text, Before and after, Video, Slideshow) run edge to edge; text sections keep their text to a readable width inside. Full width with margins : the whole screen less the side margins of the header. The section's edges line up with the header's at every width, and with the floating header card when the header floats. Page width : stops at the Page width of Theme settings, Layout , with its side margin, so the section lines up with the product, collection and search pages. The setting replaces the width settings that some sections used to have on their own (Before and after, Image, Image with text, Lookbook, Custom Liquid, Slideshow, Video and Apps)."},{"t":"The header over a section","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#transparent-header","x":"With Header behavior set to Transparent at top (the default) or Adaptive in the Header section, the header can lie over the first section of a page, transparent, in the colors that suit what is under it. See Automatic header colors . Hero, Slideshow, Video, Products showcase and Brand story hero carry Allow transparent header . When the section is first on the page, the header lies over it and starts transparent. The extra top padding settings keep your content clear of the header only while it is transparent. Many other sections carry Header over this section , off by default: Contact, FAQ, Image, Page, Rich text, Multicolumn, Routine, Key ingredients, Key figures, Bento, Scroll-revealed text, Featured product, Before and after, Collection list, Compare products, Custom Liquid, Logo list, Blog, Blog post, 404, List of collections and Collection. Checked on the first section of the template, the section's background (color, gradient or image) runs up behind the announcement bar and the header, and its content starts under the header. The Product section has neither. In its Product gradient background mode, Extend the background under the header plays that part: see Extend the gradi"},{"t":"Text colors","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#text-colors","x":"Most recent sections have a Text colors setting. Color scheme keeps the text of the section's scheme. Auto reads the real background of the section (its color, gradient or picture) and keeps the scheme's text when it reaches a contrast of 4.5:1 there, otherwise switches to white or black, for the text, icons, lines and buttons. Pick Auto when a section background makes the scheme's text hard to read."},{"t":"Inner panel and text color","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#inner-panel","x":"The About page sections and Contact place their content on an inner panel, the layer between the background and the text: Solid uses the color and opacity you set, Glass uses the shared glass recipe, Hidden removes it. Text color left on None lets the section work out a readable color from the background and the panel; pick a color only to force one."},{"t":"Heading level","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#heading-level","x":"Search engines and screen readers expect exactly one main heading (H1) per page. Sections that often open a page (Hero, FAQ, Contact, Featured set, Store locator, Brand story hero) let you choose Main heading (H1) or a subheading level. The templates that open with one of them already set H1; keep H2 anywhere else. Product, collection, blog and page templates set their own H1."},{"t":"Text left empty","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#translated-defaults","x":"Many text settings say Leave empty to use the translated default . Left empty, they show a built in text that is already translated into every language the theme ships (English, French, German, Italian and Spanish). Typing your own text replaces it in every language, so on a multilingual store either leave these fields empty or translate your text with the Translate & Adapt app. See Translations ."},{"t":"Spam protection notice","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#spam-notice","x":"Shopify protects the contact and newsletter forms with hCaptcha, which must be disclosed. Balm prints the required sentence, with its two links, under each form, which removes the hCaptcha badge from the corner of the page. The Spam protection notice settings only change its size, color and alignment."},{"t":"Header and footer","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#header-and-footer","x":"These sections live in the header and footer groups, shared by every page of the store."},{"t":"Announcement bar","p":"Sections / Header and footer","u":"sections.html#s-announcement-bar","x":"Where Header group only. A thin bar above the header, made of Message blocks. With two messages or more they rotate on their own, with optional previous and next arrows, and each message can link somewhere. With Show close button on, visitors can dismiss the bar for the rest of their visit. Display set to Scroll continuously runs the messages across the bar in a loop, like the Marquee section: Scrolling speed in pixels per second, Direction , a Separator between the messages (Dot, Dash or Custom text), Pause on hover and a pause button for visitors. Keyboard focus on a link stops the band and brings the link into view. Visitors who ask for reduced motion see the messages standing still, centred, on as many lines as they need. It works in every layout and style of the bar, Floating, Glass and Content color Auto included. Scroll behavior keeps the bar pinned, lets it scroll away with the page, or hides it on the way down and brings it back on the way up. Bar layout set to Floating turns it into a card that matches the floating header, and Bar style set to Glass uses the shared glass recipe. A floating bar sits over the first section when the header is transparent there. Use the heade","l":"Bar layout | Bar style | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Content color | Corner radius (desktop) | Corner radius (mobile) | Direction | Display | Match the header corner radius | Pause on hover | Rotation delay | Scroll behavior | Scrolling speed | Separator | Separator text | Show a pause button | Show announcement bar | Show arrows | Show close button | Space before the header (desktop) | Space before the header (mobile) | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top margin (desktop) | Top margin (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Use the header's colors over dark backgrounds"},{"t":"Block: Message","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Announcement bar","u":"sections.html#s-announcement-bar-message","x":"One message, with an optional link that makes the whole message clickable.","l":"Link | Message"},{"t":"Header","p":"Sections / Header and footer","u":"sections.html#s-header","x":"Where Header group only. The logo, the main menu, predictive search, the account and cart icons, country and language selectors, and on desktop the icons of your social media profiles ( Show social media icons , which uses the links of Theme settings, Social media ). The logo is an image, or a text wordmark set in the heading font. On phones the menu opens as a sheet under the header or as a full height drawer. Header behavior sets how the header sits on the page: Standard : the header always shows its card, in its color scheme. Transparent at top , the default: over a first section that allows it (see The header over a section ), the header is transparent, in the colors that suit that section, then takes its card on scroll. Adaptive : the header stays transparent or glass at every scroll position, on every page, and its colors and logo follow the section under it. Background when scrolled picks Glass or Transparent. Card background sets the card of Standard, and of Transparent at top once the page scrolls: Solid, in the header color scheme, or Glass. Floating header (detached) pulls the header away from the screen edges as a rounded card, with its own top margin, side margins and "},{"t":"Automatic header colors","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Header","u":"sections.html#s-header-tone","x":"With Transparent at top or Adaptive, the header works out on its own whether what lies under it is light or dark, with nothing to set per section. It reads the backgrounds painted under its middle line (colors, gradients by their stops, product gradients) and lets the color or the surface that covers most of its width decide. Over a picture or a video, it reads a small thumbnail of the part under the header, overlay included. It reads again as the page scrolls, as a slideshow changes slide and as a Products showcase wipes to the next spotlight. Over a light background, the header keeps its own Color scheme and its main Logo image . Over a dark background, it takes Colors over dark backgrounds , a color scheme with light text (Scheme 2 by default), and swaps in the Logo for dark backgrounds when you upload one. The text color goes to the menu links, the icons, the cart count, the text logo and the focus ring. An open mega menu, search panel or mobile menu always keeps the standard colors. A floating announcement bar can follow the header with Use the header's colors over dark backgrounds ."},{"t":"Example: white logo and white text over a dark image","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Header","u":"sections.html#s-header-transparent-colors","x":"In the first section of the page, for example a Hero with a dark image, turn on Allow transparent header . In the Header section, keep Header behavior on Transparent at top . Upload the white version of your logo in Logo for dark backgrounds . Your usual logo stays in Logo image . Set Colors over dark backgrounds to a scheme with white text, such as Scheme 2 of the Balm preset (white on near black). If a floating announcement bar sits over the same image, tick Use the header's colors over dark backgrounds in the Announcement bar section, so its text turns white with the header. At the top of the page the logo, the menu and the icons are white over the dark image. On scroll the header takes its card with your usual logo and colors, and the announcement bar returns to its own scheme at the same moment. Mega menu panels follow the header. With Mega menu surface on Match header, the default, they turn glass over a glass header, and the header card and the open panel form one surface at the opacity you set, so nothing of the page reads through. Under a solid header the panels stay opaque. Set Mega menu surface to Solid to keep opaque panels under a glass header too."},{"t":"Country and language selectors","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Header","u":"sections.html#s-header-localization","x":"Country and language selectors adds them to the header: Both (the default), Country/region only, Language only, or Off. On desktop a globe sits just before the search, account and cart icons, at their size, stroke and colors, the transparent header colors included. Selector style shows the globe alone (Icon only) or followed by the current language and currency codes, such as EN · USD (Icon and code). A click opens a panel in the material of the mega menu: a Country/region list that gives each country's currency, with a search field once there are more than ten countries, and a Language list. The current country and language are checked. The panel hangs under the header, aligned on the globe. While a transparent header sits at rest over the first section, with no background drawn, it opens just under the globe instead, and an open panel follows the header as it materializes on scroll. On phones and tablets the selectors sit at the bottom of the mobile menu, sheet or drawer, as a compact row of buttons that each open their own list. Choosing a country or a language reloads the same page with it. A selector shows only when there is a choice to make: the country selector needs at leas","l":"Account icon | Background when scrolled | Card background | Cart icon | Color scheme | Colors over dark backgrounds | Country and language selectors | Customer account menu | Enable predictive search | Floating corner radius (desktop) | Floating corner radius (mobile) | Floating header (detached) | Floating side margins (desktop) | Floating side margins (mobile) | Floating top margin (desktop) | Floating top margin (mobile) | Follow the global corner radius | Header behavior | Header vertical padding (desktop) | Header vertical padding (mobile) | Icon size (desktop) | Icon size (mobile) | Logo for dark backgrounds | Logo image | Logo link | Logo text | Logo type | Logo width (desktop) | Logo width (mobile) | Max thumbnail width (desktop) | Mega menu alignment (desktop) | Mega menu color scheme | Mega menu surface | Menu | Mobile menu style | Panel corner radius (desktop) | Panel corner radius (mobile) | Results per resource type | Search placeholder | Selector style | Show a background behind the thumbnail | Show cart icon | Show collections in results | Show product tagline | Show social media icons | Sticky header | Stroke width (desktop, value / 10) | Stroke width (mobile, value / 10) | Surface opacity when the menu is open (desktop) | Surface opacity when the menu is open (mobile) | Thumbnail background color | Thumbnail size | Wordmark size (desktop) | Wordmark size (mobile)"},{"t":"Footer","p":"Sections / Header and footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer","x":"Where Footer group only. The footer is a row of blocks: Large logo , Brand / logo , Link column (one of your menus), Newsletter , Social media links (the icons of your profiles and the Follow on Shop button), Text and Localization (country or currency, and language selectors, shown only when there is more than one choice). Each block sets its own width and margins for desktop and mobile. The Large logo always takes a row of its own, wherever it sits among the blocks. Under Typography , Column heading size and Link size each have a desktop and a mobile value (14 and 13 px by default). They are fluid like every text size of the theme: the desktop value applies from 1440 px wide and moves toward the mobile value on narrower screens. An optional Top decorative band draws a curve, a wave, a diagonal or your own image where the footer meets the section above. The Copyright bar at the bottom can take its own color scheme. Newsletter sign ups are added to your Shopify customers, with the tag you choose. Typical use. The store name as a large wordmark across the footer, then the logo and tagline, Shop and Help link columns, a newsletter block, and a localization block for a store that sells","l":"Band height (desktop) | Band height (mobile) | Block distribution (desktop) | Block distribution (mobile) | Color scheme | Column heading size (desktop) | Column heading size (mobile) | Copyright bar color scheme | Copyright bar colors | Copyright text | Custom image | Flip shape vertically | Horizontal spacing between blocks | Link size (desktop) | Link size (mobile) | Padding bottom (desktop) | Padding bottom (mobile) | Padding top (desktop) | Padding top (mobile) | Shape | Shape color | Show copyright bar at bottom | Show top decorative band | Vertical padding (desktop) | Vertical padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Large logo","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer-large-logo","x":"A large logo across the whole footer, on a row of its own. It comes first in the footer the theme ships with, and one footer holds one Large logo. Text , the default, sets the store name, or the Text you type, in the heading font, with the case, weight and style of Theme settings, Typography. The size is worked out so the letters fill the width on one line, and follows the width as the screen changes. Image takes your own artwork. Use an SVG, served as it is, or a transparent PNG at least 3000 px wide, so the logo stays sharp across a large screen; a PNG or JPG is served up to 3840 px wide. Recolor SVG draws a single color SVG in the color you choose; other images keep their own colors. Fill Alt text only when the header logo does not already give the store name: left empty, screen readers skip the image. Width lines the logo up with the footer columns (Content width) or runs it from one edge of the screen to the other (Full width). Alignment only has an effect when the logo is narrower than the row, which a fitted text or an image at full width never is. Crop bottom hides up to half of the logo's height, so it looks cut off by the edge of the footer. Color takes the text color of ","l":"Alignment | Alt text | Color | Crop bottom | Custom color | Logo image | Logo type | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Opacity | Recolor SVG | Show on mobile | Text | Width"},{"t":"Block: Brand / logo","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer-brand","x":"Your logo, or the store name when no logo is set, with an optional tagline. Spacing","l":"Logo image | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Tagline (optional) | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Link column","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer-link-column","x":"A heading and one of your menus. Spacing","l":"Header | Heading spacing (desktop) | Heading spacing (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Menu | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Newsletter","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer-newsletter","x":"An email sign up field. Subscribers are added to your customers with the tag you set, which email apps such as Klaviyo or Mailchimp can read. Spam protection notice Email field Spacing","l":"Customer tag for subscribers | Field maximum width (desktop) | Field maximum width (mobile) | Heading spacing (desktop) | Heading spacing (mobile) | Input placeholder | Label | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Minimum column width (desktop) | Notice alignment | Notice color | Notice text size (desktop) | Notice text size (mobile) | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Social media links","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer-social","x":"The icons of the profiles typed in Theme settings, Social media , only the networks with a URL, and the Follow on Shop button, which Shopify shows only on stores that use the Shop sales channel. Spacing","l":"Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Show the Follow on Shop button | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Text","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer-text","x":"A heading and rich text, for an address or a short note. Spacing","l":"Body | Heading | Heading spacing (desktop) | Heading spacing (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Localization","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer-localization","x":"Country or currency, and language selectors. Each appears only when your markets and languages offer more than one choice. Spacing","l":"Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Show country / currency selector | Show language selector | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Hero and storytelling","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#hero-and-storytelling","x":"Large visual sections, usually at the top of the home page or of a landing page."},{"t":"Hero","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-hero","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A full screen image or Shopify hosted video with a title and a button. Desktop and mobile each get their own image and video, cropped on the focal point you set in the admin. Video playback covers autoplay per device, a sound button, what happens at the end (loop, stop, or show the cover again), and the style and position of the controls. The cover always paints first, the video fades in over it, and the controls appear with the video, never before it. While the video loads has two styles. Cover image, then fade , the default, shows the cover sharp until the video plays. Blurred cover, then fade keeps the cover blurred until then. The hero has no loader of its own: for a loading screen, turn on the Page loader in Theme settings, Loader. A hero set to a loader style in a preview version of Balm now shows Cover image, then fade. The text block is placed separately on desktop and mobile, with a fine vertical offset, over an optional darkening overlay. Height mode (desktop) and Height mode (mobile) fit the screen, adapt to the content or take a custom height. Typical use. The first section of the home page: a short muted ","l":"Allow transparent header | Autoplay (desktop) | Autoplay (mobile) | Button background (hover) | Button label | Button link | Button style | Button text color (hover) | Color scheme | Controls position (desktop) | Controls position (mobile) | Controls style (desktop) | Controls style (mobile) | Custom height (desktop) | Custom height (mobile) | Eyebrow | Fine vertical offset | Heading | Heading level | Height mode (desktop) | Height mode (mobile) | Hero image (mobile) | Hero image (overrides bundled default) | Horizontal alignment | Media type | Overlay color | Overlay opacity | Section width | Shopify-hosted video | Shopify-hosted video (mobile) | Sound | Subheading | Transparent header top padding (desktop) | Transparent header top padding (mobile) | Vertical position | When the video ends | While the video loads"},{"t":"Slideshow","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-slideshow","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A carousel of Slide blocks. Each slide has its own desktop and mobile image, color scheme and overlay, a heading and subtext placed in one of nine positions, and up to two buttons in Solid, Outline or Glass style. Slides change on their own or on demand, with a slide or fade transition, arrows and dots. Typical use. Two to four campaigns at the top of the home page: a new product, a seasonal collection and a bundle offer. Section background More settings More settings Height Behavior Transparent header Spacing","l":"Allow transparent header | Autoplay | Autoplay delay | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Carousel accessibility label | Color scheme | Corner radius (desktop) | Corner radius (mobile) | Custom height (desktop) | Custom height (mobile) | Gradient style | Grain | Section width | Show arrows (desktop) | Show arrows (mobile) | Show dots | Slide height (desktop) | Slide height (mobile) | Space under a transparent header (desktop) | Space under a transparent header (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Transition"},{"t":"Block: Slide","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Slideshow","u":"sections.html#s-slideshow-slide","x":"One slide: images, overlay, heading, subtext, content position and up to two buttons. Content Buttons","l":"Background color | Color scheme | Content position | First button label | First button link | First button style | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Image (desktop) | Image (mobile) | Image fit (desktop) | Image fit (mobile) | Image position (desktop) | Image position (mobile) | Image size (desktop) | Image size (mobile) | Overlay opacity | Second button label | Second button link | Second button style | Subtext"},{"t":"Products showcase","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-products-showcase","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. Full screen product Spotlight blocks that take over the screen one after another. On desktop a scroll pinned wipe reveals the next product as the visitor scrolls, progressively or with a snap and a pause; phones get the same animation with a layout of their own, or a simple vertical stack. When animations are off, or the visitor asks for reduced motion, spotlights stack. The animation library loads only when the section comes near the screen. One spotlight presents one product. Pick it in Product and the spotlight fills itself: the product's title as the name, linked to its page, its custom.tagline metafield as the tagline, its custom.background_color and custom.background_color_end metafields as the background gradient, and its main image. Show the price adds the price under the tagline. On phones the product picture never covers the name, the tagline or the price: on a short screen it gets smaller to fit between them and the button. The button opens the product page; with Action set to Add to cart, a product with a single variant goes to the cart in one click and the cart drawer opens, while a product with options, ","l":"Allow transparent header | Animate the aurora slowly | Animate the spotlights on scroll | Animation on mobile | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Content offset (mobile) | Content vertical alignment (mobile) | Glow horizontal position on desktop | Glow horizontal position on mobile | Glow size on desktop | Glow size on mobile | Glow vertical position on desktop | Glow vertical position on mobile | Gradient angle | Gradient style | Grain | Heading hover color | Heading hover effect | Hide the header during this section (desktop) | Hide the header during this section (mobile) | Horizontal offset (desktop) | Horizontal offset (mobile) | Image size (desktop) | Image size (mobile) | Ingredients (one per line) | Pause between spotlights | Pause per spotlight | Scroll mode | Scroll per wipe | Section width | Size subtitle | Space under a transparent header (desktop) | Space under a transparent header (mobile) | Spinning badge | Text color | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Vertical alignment (desktop) | Vertical alignment (mobile) | Vertical offset (desktop) | Vertical offset (mobile) | Wipe direction"},{"t":"Block: Spotlight","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Products showcase","u":"sections.html#s-products-showcase-spotlight","x":"One product spotlight: the product that fills it, the override fields, the image size and position, the Shop now or Add to cart button, highlights, the featured set cartouche, visibility and watermark. Override (optional) Image size and position Button Highlights · Heading Highlights · Claims Highlights · Layout Featured set Cartouche thumbnail Cartouche style Visibility Watermark Spinning badge","l":"Action | Alignment (desktop) | Alignment (mobile) | Background color | Background color end | Border color | Border width | Button label | Cartouche corners | Cartouche heading | Cartouche link | Cartouche position | Cartouche small text | Cartouche style | Cartouche thumbnail | Center content | Claim 1 icon | Claim 1 text | Claim 2 icon | Claim 2 text | Claim 3 icon | Claim 3 text | Claim 4 icon | Claim 4 text | Claim icon size (desktop) | Claim icon size (mobile) | Claims gap (desktop) | Claims gap (mobile) | Claims row alignment (desktop) | Color scheme | Corner radius | Custom width (desktop) | Custom width (mobile) | Direction | Earlier claim 1 text | Earlier claim 2 text | Earlier claim 3 text | Earlier claim 4 text | Glyph | Heading | Heading and group alignment (desktop) | Heading and group alignment (mobile) | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Horizontal offset (desktop) | Horizontal offset (mobile) | Horizontal padding (desktop) | Horizontal padding (mobile) | Horizontal position (desktop) | Horizontal position (mobile) | Icon and text gap (desktop) | Icon and text gap (mobile) | Icon size | Image | Image fit | Image size (desktop) | Image size (mobile) | Letter spacing (desktop) | Letter spacing (mobile) | Link | Long text | Name | Number of claims | One full turn | Opacity | Orientation | Place behind the product | Placement (desktop) | Placement (mobile) | Product | Repeat text | Rotate | Separator | Shape | Show cartouche on | Show featured-set cartouche | Show highlights on | Show on | Show on mobile | Show the price | Show thumbnail | Size | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Small text size (desktop) | Small text size (mobile) | Start angle | Style | Tagline | Text | Text case | Text color | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Thumbnail corners | Thumbnail padding (desktop) | Thumbnail padding (mobile) | Thumbnail position (desktop) | Thumbnail position (mobile) | Thumbnail ratio | Thumbnail size (desktop) | Thumbnail size (mobile) | Type | Use a custom size and position | Use its own color scheme | Vertical alignment (desktop) | Vertical alignment (mobile) | Vertical direction | Vertical offset (desktop) | Vertical offset (mobile) | Vertical padding (desktop) | Vertical padding (mobile) | Vertical position (desktop) | Vertical position (mobile) | Watermark size (desktop) | Watermark size (mobile) | Weight | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Featured set","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-featured-set","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. One product, usually a bundle or a discovery set, presented as a full width banner: a heading, a tagline in two parts and an add to cart button. Pick the Product and the section fills itself: its title as the heading, its custom.tagline metafield as the tagline, its custom.background_color metafield as the background, and its image. The button adds that product to the cart. Each field of the Override (optional) group replaces one of those values: leave a field empty to use the product's value, and a background that neither gives takes the color scheme's. Tagline, second part has no product value: it shows only what you type. Your own desktop and mobile background images replace the product image, darkened by an optional overlay. Until a product is picked, the section shows a placeholder in the editor and nothing on the storefront. See Metafields . Typical use. Promoting a discovery set at the top of the Products page template (page.products), which opens with this section. Override (optional) Text Colors This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Background color | Background image | Background image (mobile) | Button label | Color scheme | Heading | Heading level | Overlay color | Overlay opacity | Product | Section width | Show the product image | Tagline | Tagline, second part"},{"t":"Image","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-image","x":"Where Only on * templates. One picture, with an optional Image (mobile) shown under 768 px. Each picture shows at its own focal point, and a phone downloads only its own. Ratio (desktop) and Ratio (mobile) keep the picture's own shape (Original) or set one (1:1, 4:5, 3:2, 16:9, 21:9 or a custom height), with Fit to fill or contain. A link, a corner radius, a border, an overlay and a Scroll animation (Fade in, Zoom out or Parallax, never for visitors who ask for reduced motion) complete it. Visibility shows it on both devices, desktop only or mobile only. Add a Caption block for a line of text under the picture. As the first section of a page, the picture loads at once, with a high priority. With Section width on Full width and Header over this section checked, the header lies over the picture and reads its tone. Typical use. A wide lifestyle photo between two sections of the home page, or a campaign visual at the top of a landing page, with a lighter crop for phones. Media Layout Style Animation and visibility Section background More settings More settings More settings Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Border width | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Corner radius | Custom height (desktop) | Custom height (mobile) | Fit (when a ratio is set) | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Image | Image (mobile) | Link | Overlay color | Overlay opacity | Ratio (desktop) | Ratio (mobile) | Scroll animation | Section width | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Visibility"},{"t":"Block: Caption","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Image","u":"sections.html#s-image-caption","x":"A short text under the picture, with its size per device, its alignment and its spacing. Text color left empty takes a color that reads on the section background.","l":"Alignment | Text | Text color | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Text top spacing (desktop) | Text top spacing (mobile)"},{"t":"Image with text","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-image-with-text","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. An image beside a content column you build from theme blocks : headings, text, buttons, images, spacers and custom Liquid. Choose the image side on desktop, the order on mobile, the image width and ratio, and the gap. Translucent card (glass) lets the content card overlap the image on desktop. Typical use. Telling the brand story or explaining one product benefit, with a photo, a heading, two short paragraphs and a button. Layout Image Glass style Content Section background More settings More settings This section accepts the theme blocks (Heading, Text, Button, Image, Spacer, Liquid).","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Content inner padding (desktop) | Content inner padding (mobile) | Corner radius | Fit (when a ratio is set) | Gradient style | Image | Image / text gap (desktop) | Image / text gap (mobile) | Image position (desktop) | Image width (desktop) | Inner panel color | Inner panel opacity | Minimum height (desktop) | Minimum height (mobile) | Order (mobile) | Overlap (desktop) | Ratio | Section width | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Translucent card (glass)"},{"t":"Rich text","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-rich-text","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A single column of theme blocks (headings, text, buttons, images, spacers, custom Liquid) in a narrow, normal or wide measure, aligned separately on desktop and mobile. Background set to Transparent lets the section sit on the page without its own fill. Typical use. A brand statement between two visual sections, or an introduction paragraph at the top of a landing page. Section background More settings More settings More settings This section accepts the theme blocks (Heading, Text, Button, Image, Spacer, Liquid).","l":"Background | Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Content alignment (desktop) | Content alignment (mobile) | Content width | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Inner padding (desktop) | Inner padding (mobile) | Section width | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Scroll-revealed text","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-scroll-text","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. One strong statement whose words light up one after another as it scrolls into view. Type it in Text ; a line break starts a new paragraph, and words between asterisks, *like this* , are highlighted in the Highlight style you pick: Italic, Accent color or Underline. Strength of unread words sets how faint the words are before they light up; it is raised automatically when needed, so they always keep a contrast of 3:1 with the background. Visitors who ask for reduced motion, and browsers without scroll animations, see every word lit at once. Typical use. The brand promise in two short sentences between the hero and the products, with two key words highlighted. Heading and intro Text Section background More settings More settings More settings Spacing","l":"Alignment | Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Heading | Heading alignment | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Highlight style | Intro | Section width | Strength of unread words | Text | Text colors | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Text width | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Bento","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-bento","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A grid of tiles of different sizes: four columns on desktop, two on phones. Add Image tile , Text tile , Product tile , Stat tile and Video tile blocks, and give each a Size (desktop) and a Size (mobile) of one or two columns and one or two rows. Order on mobile moves a tile forward on phones without changing the desktop order. Row height , Card gap and Corner radius set the grid; rows grow when a tile, such as a product card, needs more room. Typical use. A home page block that mixes a large lifestyle photo, a best seller, a key figure such as 98% natural origin and a short brand text. Heading and intro Layout Section background More settings More settings More settings Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Color scheme | Corner radius | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Heading | Heading alignment | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Intro | Row height (desktop) | Row height (mobile) | Section width | Text colors | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Image tile","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Bento","u":"sections.html#s-bento-image","x":"A picture with an optional heading over it, in white over a dark gradient, and an optional link. Size and order","l":"Heading | Image | Link | Order on mobile | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Text tile","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Bento","u":"sections.html#s-bento-text","x":"A heading, a text and an optional button, on a color scheme of its own (Scheme 2 by default). Size and order","l":"Button label | Button link | Color scheme | Heading | Order on mobile | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Text"},{"t":"Block: Product tile","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Bento","u":"sections.html#s-bento-product","x":"A product card, with its own Badges setting (All, Automatic only, Custom only or None). Size and order","l":"Badges | Order on mobile | Product | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Stat tile","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Bento","u":"sections.html#s-bento-stat","x":"A large number and its label, on a color scheme of its own. Size and order","l":"Color scheme | Label | Number | Order on mobile | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Video tile","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Bento","u":"sections.html#s-bento-video","x":"A video uploaded to Shopify. It plays muted, with its controls, only when the visitor starts it. Size and order","l":"Order on mobile | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Video"},{"t":"Video","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-video","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A video from Shopify (uploaded in the admin) or from YouTube or Vimeo, with its own mobile source. External videos load as a click to play cover: nothing from the third party loads before the click. Shopify videos can instead play muted on a loop with no controls. Choose the aspect ratio, full width or a maximum width, and an optional heading. Typical use. A one minute brand film on the About page, or a muted loop of the product being prepared on the home page. Section background More settings More settings Content Video source Layout Spacing Transparent header","l":"Allow transparent header | Aspect ratio | Autoplay muted loop (Shopify video only) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Custom cover image | External video URL | External video URL (mobile) | Gradient style | Grain | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Maximum width (desktop) | Section width | Shopify-hosted video | Shopify-hosted video (mobile) | Space under a transparent header (desktop) | Space under a transparent header (mobile) | Start with sound | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Marquee","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-marquee","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A band of text that scrolls across the screen. Type one message per line; the separator you pick (a dot, a dash, your own text or a small image) is inserted between them automatically. Set the speed, the direction and the height, and keep the pause button on: accessibility guidelines ask for one on any animation that runs by itself. Typical use. Short claims between two sections, such as Free delivery from 40 euros, Vegan, Made in France. Separator Section background More settings More settings More settings Size Spacing","l":"Animation speed (seconds per cycle) | Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Direction | Font size (desktop) | Font size (mobile) | Gradient style | Grain | Height (desktop) | Height (mobile) | Messages | Section width | Separator | Separator image | Separator image height (desktop) | Separator image height (mobile) | Separator text | Show a pause button | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Before and after","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-before-after","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. Two images stacked on top of each other with a handle the visitor drags to compare them, horizontally or vertically. Add labels, a starting position, a round handle or a plain line, a heading and text. The handle also works from the keyboard, through a slider. Typical use. Showing the result of a product: a surface before and after cleaning, skin before and after four weeks, a room before and after. Content Images Comparison Layout Section background More settings More settings More settings Spacing","l":"After image | After image (mobile) | After label | Background image (mobile) | Before image | Before image (mobile) | Before label | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Content alignment | Gradient style | Grain | Handle style | Header over this section | Heading | Image ratio | Image ratio (mobile) | Orientation | Section width | Starting position | Text | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Products and collections","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#products-and-collections","x":"Sections that show products or collections and let shoppers buy from them."},{"t":"Featured product","p":"Sections / Products and collections","u":"sections.html#s-featured-product","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. One product, picked in Product , presented on any page with the blocks of the product page: title, price, variant picker, Buy buttons with the quantity and Buy it now, description, collapsible rows and the others, plus the theme blocks and app blocks. Its media show in a gallery: images, Shopify hosted videos, YouTube and Vimeo videos and 3D models with the AR button, with the gallery arrows of Theme settings, Carousels . Choosing a variant updates the price and shows the variant's image, without changing the page address. Add to cart opens the cart as Theme settings, Cart says. Without a product, the theme editor shows a placeholder and nothing shows on the storefront. Typical use. Launching a new product on the home page, with its gallery, its variant picker and Add to cart, two sections under the hero. Layout Media Section background More settings More settings More settings Spacing This section accepts the theme blocks (Heading, Text, Button, Image, Spacer, Liquid) and accepts app blocks.","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Fit (when a ratio is set) | Gallery arrows | Gallery width (desktop) | Gap between columns (desktop) | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Media controls style | Media corner radius | Media position (desktop) | Media ratio | Order (mobile) | Product | Section width | Show the AR button on 3D models | Space between media and text (mobile) | Text colors | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Featured collection","p":"Sections / Products and collections","u":"sections.html#s-featured-collection","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A grid of products from one collection, with the full product card: second image on hover, quick add, quick view, badges, vendor and a button. Promo tile blocks take the place of a card at the position you choose, and a View all button can link to the collection. Typical use. Best sellers on the home page: four products, quick add on, a promo tile in third position and a View all button. Section background More settings More settings More settings Content Layout Cards Card button View all button Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button alignment | Button horizontal padding (desktop) | Button horizontal padding (mobile) | Button label | Button style | Button text size (desktop) | Button text size (mobile) | Button vertical padding (desktop) | Button vertical padding (mobile) | Card button label | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Collection | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Element order | Gradient style | Grain | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Image fit | Image ratio | Maximum products | Product title to price spacing (desktop) | Product title to price spacing (mobile) | Quick add | Quick add label | Quick view | Second image on hover | Section width | Show the \"View all\" button | Show vendor | Spacing inside card (desktop) | Spacing inside card (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Promo tile","p":"Sections / Products and collections / Featured collection","u":"sections.html#s-featured-collection-promo-tile","x":"A tile that takes the place of a product card at the position you choose, on the first page of the grid only.","l":"Button label | Color scheme | Heading | Image | Image (mobile) | Link | Position in the grid | Text | Text alignment | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Collection list","p":"Sections / Products and collections","u":"sections.html#s-collection-list","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. Cards for the collections you pick with Collection blocks, with their image, title and an optional product count. Set the columns, the gap, the image ratio and fit. Typical use. A Shop by category row on the home page with three or four collections. Section background More settings More settings More settings Content Layout Cards Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Card title size (desktop) | Card title size (mobile) | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Image fit | Image ratio | Section width | Show product count | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Collection","p":"Sections / Products and collections / Collection list","u":"sections.html#s-collection-list-collection","x":"One collection card.","l":"Collection"},{"t":"Routine","p":"Sections / Products and collections","u":"sections.html#s-routine","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A care routine, step by step. Each Step block holds a step label, a product, a short text and a moment: Morning, Evening, or both. With Show Morning and Evening tabs , two tabs show the steps of one moment at a time; they appear only when at least one step is for a single moment. Show the total price adds the price of the moment's products, and the button adds them all to the cart in one go, then opens the cart as Theme settings, Cart says. It works without JavaScript too. Columns and Card style set the layout. Second image on hover crossfades to the step's Image on hover , or to the product's second image. Typical use. A Morning and evening routine of four products (cleanser, serum, cream and night balm) on a product page or the home page, with Add the routine. Heading and intro Layout Section background More settings More settings More settings Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Card style | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Heading | Heading alignment | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Intro | Second image on hover | Section width | Show Morning and Evening tabs | Show the total price | Text colors | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Step","p":"Sections / Products and collections / Routine","u":"sections.html#s-routine-step","x":"One step of the routine: a Step label (the number of the step when empty), a product, an optional Image that replaces the product's, a short text and its Moment : Morning and evening, Morning or Evening.","l":"Image | Image on hover | Moment | Product | Step label | Text"},{"t":"Lookbook","p":"Sections / Products and collections","u":"sections.html#s-lookbook","x":"Where Any template, and the header and footer groups. An image with Hotspot blocks. Each hotspot points at a product or shows a text; on desktop it opens a popover with the product card and its quick add, on a phone a sheet from the bottom of the screen. The Image with product list layout lines the products up as cards beside the image, and hovering a card lights its hotspot. Hotspots have separate desktop and mobile positions. Typical use. Shop the look: a styled photo of three products used together, each one clickable and addable to the cart. Section background More settings More settings More settings Content Image Layout Hotspots Product cards Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card image ratio | Color scheme | Gradient style | Grain | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Hotspot color | Hotspot colors | Hotspot icon | Hotspot icon color | Hotspot shape | Hotspot size (desktop) | Hotspot size (mobile) | Hotspot style | Image | Image (mobile) | Image ratio | Layout | Product list position | Quick add | Quick add label | Quick view | Section width | Text | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Hotspot","p":"Sections / Products and collections / Lookbook","u":"sections.html#s-lookbook-hotspot","x":"One point on the image, linked to a product or carrying a text, with its desktop and mobile position. Position (desktop) Position (mobile)","l":"Content | Heading | Horizontal position | Link | Link label | Product | Text | Vertical position"},{"t":"Compare products","p":"Sections / Products and collections","u":"sections.html#s-compare-products","x":"Where Any template, and the header and footer groups. Up to five products side by side. Built in rows show the image, the badges, the price, the availability, the vendor and the rating. Each Row block adds a line: its Label sits in the left column, and its value is read on every compared product from its Source : Metafield, Vendor, Product type, Tags, SKU, Barcode, Weight or Unit price. With Metafield, type the metafield's name as in your admin (Skin type) or its key (custom.skin_type) in Metafield . Each value is drawn by its type: yes and no as icons, a list as a sentence, a number with the row's Unit , a color with its swatch, a reference by its title. Highlight differences marks the rows where products differ, and an empty value shows a hyphen. Mobile layout shows one card per product (Cards), or keeps the table with the label column in place while the product columns scroll (Scroll). See Metafields, Compare products rows for an example. Typical use. Comparing the three creams of a range on their key facts: texture, skin type and whether they are fragrance free. Section background More settings More settings More settings Content Rows Product cards Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Column width (mobile) | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Highlight differences | Mobile layout | Products | Quick add | Quick add label | Section width | Show availability | Show price | Show product image | Show rating | Show vendor | Text | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Row","p":"Sections / Products and collections / Compare products","u":"sections.html#s-compare-products-row","x":"One comparison line: a Label , and a Source read on every compared product (a metafield by its name or key, the vendor, the product type, the tags, the SKU, the barcode, the weight or the unit price). See Metafields .","l":"Label | Metafield | Source | Unit"},{"t":"Recently viewed","p":"Sections / Products and collections","u":"sections.html#s-recently-viewed","x":"Where Any template, and the header and footer groups. The products the visitor opened most recently, newest first. The list is kept in the visitor's own browser, so it needs no app and no account; the section takes no space until there is a history. The theme editor shows example cards instead. Typical use. At the bottom of product pages, with the current product excluded, or on the cart page. Section background More settings More settings More settings Content Layout Cards Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card button label | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Exclude the current product | Gradient style | Grain | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Image fit | Image ratio | Maximum products | Mobile layout | Quick add | Quick add label | Quick view | Second image on hover | Section width | Show vendor | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Trust and engagement","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#trust-and-engagement","x":"Reassurance, proof, social proof and ways to stay in touch."},{"t":"Key ingredients","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-key-ingredients","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. The ingredients that make a product work, one Ingredient block each: a picture, a name, the benefit it brings and a detail. Layout (desktop) and Layout (mobile) show them as a grid, a carousel, or Auto, a carousel only when the cards outnumber the columns. The carousel uses the arrows of Theme settings, Carousels . Detail set to Over the picture shows the detail on the picture on hover or focus with a mouse, and through each ingredient's More about button on every device; set to Always under the benefit, it is always visible. Turn off Show button in an ingredient to remove its button. Image ratio takes a square, portrait, landscape or circle frame. Typical use. Three hero ingredients of a serum, each with a close up photo, the benefit in one line and where it comes from. Heading and intro Layout Section background More settings More settings More settings Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card style | Carousel navigation | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Detail | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Heading | Heading alignment | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Image ratio | Intro | Layout (desktop) | Layout (mobile) | Next card preview (mobile) | Section width | Text colors | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Ingredient","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement / Key ingredients","u":"sections.html#s-key-ingredients-ingredient","x":"One ingredient: a picture, a name, the benefit and a detail. With Show button , a More about button reveals the detail; fill Button link to make it open a page instead.","l":"Benefit | Button label | Button link | Detail | Image | Name | Show button"},{"t":"Key figures","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-key-figures","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A row of figures, one Figure block each: a number with an optional prefix and suffix, a label and a source note. Count up the numbers counts each figure up once when it scrolls into view; it works on plain numbers, such as 98 or 4.8, and never for visitors who ask for reduced motion. The real figure is always in the page for screen readers. Columns, gaps, alignment, number sizes and Card style (None, Solid, Outline or Glass) set the look. Only state figures you can prove, and say where each one comes from in its Source note . Typical use. Results of a consumer test under a product launch: 98% feel softer skin, 4.8 out of 5 average rating, 30 days of use, with the study named in the source notes. Heading and intro Layout Section background More settings More settings More settings Spacing","l":"Alignment | Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Card style | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Count up the numbers | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Heading | Heading alignment | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Intro | Number size (desktop) | Number size (mobile) | Section width | Text colors | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Figure","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement / Key figures","u":"sections.html#s-key-figures-figure","x":"One figure: the Number , an optional Prefix and Suffix (keep the unit there, so the number counts up), a Label that says what it measures and an optional Source note .","l":"Label | Number | Prefix | Source note | Suffix"},{"t":"Multicolumn","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-multicolumn","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A row of Column blocks, each with an image (square, landscape, portrait or circle), a heading, text and a link, plus an optional button for the whole section. On phones the columns stack or become a horizontal slider. Typical use. Three reasons to buy, or How it works in three steps, each with a small illustration. Section background More settings More settings More settings Content Layout Section button Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Button link | Card style | Color scheme | Column gap (desktop) | Column gap (mobile) | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Content alignment | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Icon size | Icon style | Mobile layout | Section width | Text colors | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Column","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement / Multicolumn","u":"sections.html#s-multicolumn-column","x":"One column: image, heading, text and link.","l":"Heading | Icon | Image | Image ratio | Image width (desktop) | Image width (mobile) | Link | Link label | Text"},{"t":"Testimonials","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-testimonials","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. Testimonial blocks with a quote, a star rating, an author, a role or source and an avatar, as a grid or a horizontal slider. The slider can rotate on its own; it pauses on hover and focus and stops for good once the visitor takes control. Cards are Solid, Outline or Glass. Typical use. Five short customer quotes in a slider under the product showcase, or press quotes with the name of the publication as the source. Section background More settings More settings More settings Content Layout Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card background | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Card style | Cards visible (desktop) | Change every | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Desktop layout | Gradient style | Grain | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Mobile layout | Rotate automatically | Section width | Show arrows (desktop) | Show arrows (mobile) | Text colors | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Testimonial","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement / Testimonials","u":"sections.html#s-testimonials-testimonial","x":"One testimonial card.","l":"Author | Avatar | Quote | Role or source | Star rating (0 hides stars)"},{"t":"Logo list","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-logo-list","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A row of Logo blocks with an optional heading, shown still or scrolling as a marquee. Logos can be grayscale until hovered and can each link somewhere. Typical use. An As seen in row of press logos, or the retailers that stock your products. Section background More settings More settings More settings Content Logos Marquee Spacing","l":"Alignment | Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Case | Color scheme | Gap (desktop) | Gap (mobile) | Gradient style | Grain | Grayscale (color on hover) | Header over this section | Heading | Logo height (desktop) | Logo height (mobile) | Scroll duration | Scroll logos (marquee) | Section width | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Space below heading (desktop) | Space below heading (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Weight"},{"t":"Block: Logo","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement / Logo list","u":"sections.html#s-logo-list-logo","x":"One logo, with an optional link.","l":"Link | Logo image"},{"t":"Countdown","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-countdown","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A timer counting down to a date and time in your store's timezone (format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM ), with days, hours, minutes and seconds you can show or hide and rename. When it reaches zero it shows a message or hides the section. Typical use. The last days of a sale, or the launch of a limited edition. Section background More settings More settings Content Target Units Style Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Days label | Digit size (desktop) | Digit size (mobile) | End message | Gradient style | Grain | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Hours label | Minutes label | Seconds label | Section width | Show days | Show hours | Show minutes | Show seconds | Subtext | Target date | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Unit box style | When the countdown ends"},{"t":"Newsletter","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-newsletter","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. An email sign up band with a heading and subtext, on a solid or glass panel or on no panel at all, over the section background. Sign ups are added to your Shopify customers with email marketing consent. Typical use. A 10% welcome offer above the footer, over a lifestyle photo. Section background More settings More settings More settings Content Panel Height Spam protection notice Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Content alignment | Custom height (desktop) | Custom height (mobile) | Email placeholder | Gradient style | Grain | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Height (desktop) | Height (mobile) | Notice alignment | Notice color | Notice text size (desktop) | Notice text size (mobile) | Panel style | Panel top and bottom padding (desktop) | Panel top and bottom padding (mobile) | Panel width (desktop) | Panel width (mobile) | Section width | Submit label | Subtext | Success message | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Newsletter popup","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-newsletter-popup","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. An email sign up popup that opens after a delay and comes back after the number of days you set once closed (0 shows it on every visit). The card is Tinted glass, Glass or Solid over a dimmed page. Sign ups are added to your Shopify customers with the tag newsletter . The home page template includes it; add it to other templates when you want it there too. Typical use. A welcome offer shown five seconds after arrival, once every 30 days. Content Spam protection notice","l":"Card opacity | Card style | Close button label (accessibility) | Color scheme | Email field placeholder | Enable popup | Heading | Legal text | Notice alignment | Notice color | Notice text size (desktop) | Notice text size (mobile) | Open delay | Overlay opacity (desktop) | Overlay opacity (mobile) | Reappear after | Subheading | Submit button label (accessibility) | Success message"},{"t":"Social media links","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-socials","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A heading, the icons of your social media profiles and an optional button. The icons are the links typed once in Theme settings, Social media : only the networks with a URL show. The button, outlined or in glass, appears only when Button link is filled. Previous versions of Balm named this section Socials. Typical use. An @yourbrand band with the Instagram, TikTok and Pinterest icons and a Follow us button, above the footer. Content Section background More settings More settings More settings Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Button link | Button style | Color scheme | Gap between heading and button | Gradient style | Grain | Heading | Padding bottom | Padding top | Section width | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"FAQ","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-faq","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A title column beside an accordion of FAQ item blocks (a question and a rich text answer), with an optional subheading and button. Alignment, gaps and row heights are set separately for desktop and mobile. The FAQ page template ( page.faq ) opens with it. Typical use. An FAQ page of eight to twelve questions on delivery, returns and ingredients, with a Contact us button under the title. Section background More settings More settings More settings Alignment Spacing Questions","l":"Accordion content alignment (desktop) | Accordion content alignment (mobile) | Answer bottom padding (desktop) | Answer bottom padding (mobile) | Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Button link | Button style | Button text color | Color scheme | Gap between questions (desktop) | Gap between questions (mobile) | Gap between the two columns (desktop) | Gap between the two columns (mobile) | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Heading | Heading column spacing (desktop) | Heading column spacing (mobile) | Heading level | Icon | Minimum height (desktop) | Minimum height (mobile) | Open several questions at once | Open the first question | Question background | Question row padding (desktop) | Question row padding (mobile) | Question style | Question text | Section heading alignment (desktop) | Section heading alignment (mobile) | Section width | Subheading | Text colors | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: FAQ item","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement / FAQ","u":"sections.html#s-faq-item","x":"One question and its answer.","l":"Answer | Question"},{"t":"About page","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#about-page","x":"Four sections built for a brand story page. The About template ( page.about ) opens with them, and each one can be added to any other page too."},{"t":"Brand story hero","p":"Sections / About page","u":"sections.html#s-about-hero","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. The opening section of the About page: a three part italic title, a heading, body text, a button and an image, on an inner panel over the section background. Typical use. The top of the About page, with the brand promise in the title and the founding story in two short paragraphs. Section background Panel background Transparent header Spacing","l":"Allow transparent header | Body font size | Body text | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Button link | Button style | Button text color | Color scheme | Dark overlay opacity | Gradient angle | Gradient end | Heading | Heading level | Heading part 1 (light italic) | Heading part 2 (black italic) | Heading part 3 (italic) | Inner panel color | Inner panel opacity | Inner panel style | Left image (media) | Panel image | Panel image (mobile) | Section width | Text color | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Transparent header top padding (desktop) | Transparent header top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Comparison panels","p":"Sections / About page","u":"sections.html#s-about-problem-shift","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. Two panels side by side, each with a title, a subtitle and body text, on an inner panel over the section background. Typical use. The problem on the left and how your product changes it on the right. Section background More settings More settings More settings Inner panel Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Gradient style | Grain | Inner panel color | Inner panel opacity | Inner panel style | Left body | Left heading | Left subtitle | Right body | Right heading | Right subtitle | Section width | Text color | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Checklist banner","p":"Sections / About page","u":"sections.html#s-about-feels-off","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. An interactive checklist of Check item blocks that visitors tick, beside a heading, a subheading and a button. Once items are ticked, the button leads to the link of the first or last ticked item that has one, or to the button link. Typical use. A Does this sound like you? list of four situations, each linked to the product that answers it. Section background More settings More settings Panel background Spacing","l":"Background image | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Button link | Button style | Button text color | Checklist heading | Color scheme | Dark overlay opacity | Footer text | Gradient angle | Gradient end | Gradient style | Grain | Heading | Inner panel color | Inner panel opacity | Inner panel opacity (mobile) | Inner panel style | Panel image | Panel image (mobile) | Section width | Subheading | Text color | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Check item","p":"Sections / About page / Checklist banner","u":"sections.html#s-about-feels-off-item","x":"One line of the checklist, with an optional link the button can take over.","l":"Item link (optional) | Item text"},{"t":"Gallery banner","p":"Sections / About page","u":"sections.html#s-about-community","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A background image crossed by a colored band with two large words, a link below the band, and a gallery of Element blocks (images, round or square, optionally linked) that scrolls sideways with arrows. Typical use. Photos from your community or your Instagram at the bottom of the About page. Background Colors Elements Spacing","l":"Background color | Background image | Background image (mobile) | Band color | Band opacity | Band text color | Band text size (desktop) | Band text size (mobile) | Banner word 1 | Banner word 2 | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Custom radius (desktop) | Custom radius (mobile) | Element shape | Element size (desktop) | Element size (mobile) | Link URL (below the band) | Link color (desktop) | Link color (mobile) | Link label (below the band) | Overlay color | Overlay opacity | Section width | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Element","p":"Sections / About page / Gallery banner","u":"sections.html#s-about-community-element","x":"One image of the gallery, with an optional link and its own shape.","l":"Custom radius (desktop) | Custom radius (mobile) | Image | Link (optional) | Shape"},{"t":"Contact and stores","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#contact-and-stores","x":"Used by the Contact ( page.contact ) and Store locator ( page.find-us ) templates."},{"t":"Contact","p":"Sections / Contact and stores","u":"sections.html#s-contact","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. The Shopify contact form in a card, with a heading, a subtitle and a success message. Messages reach the email address of your store. The Contact page template ( page.contact ) uses it. Typical use. The Contact page, with a subtitle that gives your response time. Section background More settings More settings More settings Inner panel Spam protection notice Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Border color | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card corner radius | Color scheme | Field background | Field corner radius | Form width (desktop) | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Heading | Heading level | Inner panel color | Inner panel opacity | Inner panel style | Name and email fields (desktop) | Notice alignment | Notice color | Notice text size (desktop) | Notice text size (mobile) | Section width | Subtitle | Success message | Text color | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Store locator","p":"Sections / Contact and stores","u":"sections.html#s-find-us","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A store locator page over a background photo: two columns of Stores and Online lists (rich text, shown as accordions), and a map slot for an app block or a Custom Liquid block where you paste a store locator embed. The Store locator template ( page.find-us ) uses it. Typical use. A Where to buy page listing your retailers city by city, with the map of a store locator app. Background Spacing Store-locator map Accordion labels Column 1 Column 2","l":"\"Online\" label | \"Stores\" label | Background image | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Column 1 (online) | Column 1 (stores) | Column 1 heading | Column 2 (online) | Column 2 (stores) | Column 2 heading | Dark overlay opacity | Gap between columns (desktop) | Heading | Heading level | Map height (desktop) | Map height (mobile) | Section width | Show second column | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Custom Liquid","p":"Sections / Contact and stores / Store locator","u":"sections.html#s-find-us-liquid","x":"Paste the embed code of a store locator service here. This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Liquid / HTML code"},{"t":"Layout, code and apps","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#layout-and-code","x":""},{"t":"Divider","p":"Sections / Layout, code and apps","u":"sections.html#s-divider","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A line or an empty space between two sections, with its own height for desktop and mobile, line thickness, width and opacity. Typical use. A thin line between two sections that share the same background. Section background More settings More settings More settings","l":"Background image (mobile) | Color scheme | Gradient style | Grain | Height (desktop) | Height (mobile) | Line opacity | Line thickness | Line width | Section width | Style"},{"t":"Custom Liquid","p":"Sections / Layout, code and apps","u":"sections.html#s-custom-liquid","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. Your own Liquid, HTML or app snippet in a section of its own, contained or full width, with the usual color scheme, background and spacing settings. Read Custom code before using it. Typical use. An embed code provided by a third party service that has no app block. Section background More settings More settings More settings","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Liquid code | Section width | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Apps","p":"Sections / Layout, code and apps","u":"sections.html#s-apps","x":"Where Any template, and the header and footer groups. A container for app blocks, with a color scheme and spacing, and an option to remove the content width limit so an app can draw edge to edge. Typical use. Reviews carousel or Instagram feed from an app, placed between two sections of the home page. Spacing This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Section width | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Template sections","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#template-sections","x":"The main section of each template: what a product, collection, cart or blog page shows. Most of them cannot be removed from their template, but their settings are yours."},{"t":"Product","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-product","x":"Where Part of the product template. The product page: media gallery on one side, a column of blocks on the other. It is the main section of the product template, so it is not offered in Add section . Preview versions of Balm also offered a second version of it there, Balm spotlight; it has been removed. Its product gradient background and its spinning badge are now a background mode of the Product section and the positions of the Spinning badge block. Its settings and every block are documented on Product page blocks ."},{"t":"Product recommendations","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-product-recommendations","x":"Where Only on product templates. Product cards under the product page. Recommendation intent picks where they come from: Related (similar products) are generated by Shopify, Complementary (pairs well with) are the ones you curate in the Search & Discovery app, and Random from a collection shows products of the Collection you pick, in a new order on every visit. Fill up from the collection completes Shopify's recommendations from that collection when they are fewer than the maximum. Neither ever shows a product twice, nor the product of the page. The cards sit in a grid or a carousel per device, with the arrows of Theme settings, Carousels , and Badges picks which badges they show. Typical use. Four related products under every product page, with the custom badge showing on new formulas. Section background More settings More settings Content Layout Cards Spacing","l":"Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card button label | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Carousel navigation (desktop) | Carousel navigation (mobile) | Collection | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Fill up from the collection | Gradient style | Grain | Heading | Image fit | Image ratio | Layout (desktop) | Layout (mobile) | Maximum products | Next card preview (mobile) | Product title to price spacing (desktop) | Product title to price spacing (mobile) | Recommendation intent | Section width | Spacing inside card (desktop) | Spacing inside card (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Sticky add to cart","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-sticky-atc","x":"Where Only on product templates. A bar with the product thumbnail, title, selected variant, price and add to cart button that stays at the top or bottom of the screen, on desktop and mobile separately. By default it appears once the main buy button scrolls out of view. A variant that sells as a pre-order says Pre-order here too. The bar exists only as this section, which the product template places below the Product section. Preview versions of Balm also offered it as a Sticky add to cart block inside the Product section; that block has been removed. Typical use. At the bottom of the screen on phones, where the main buy button quickly scrolls away. Position Displayed content Behavior Button","l":"Always visible | Bar height | Button background | Button text | Enable the bar | Position (desktop) | Position (mobile) | Price | Product thumbnail (desktop) | Product thumbnail (mobile) | Product title | Selected variant"},{"t":"Collection","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-collection","x":"Where Part of the collection template. The collection page: a banner with the title, description and image, an optional row of collection links, filters and sorting, and the product grid. Filters come from the Search & Discovery app and can sit in a column, a drawer or a horizontal bar, whose drawer style is set in Theme settings, Filters . Pagination is page numbers, a Load more button or infinite scroll. Visitors can change the column count when you allow it (see Column selector ), and Promo tile blocks take the place of a card on the first page. Badges picks the badges of the cards, and Text behind cutouts prints the product's title behind PNG and WebP pictures. It is the main section of the collection template, so it is not offered in Add section . The banner shows, in this order, the collection's custom.banner_image metafield, the Banner image set in the section, or the collection's own image. Shopify keeps no focal point on a collection's image: pick the picture in the section or in the metafield to frame it at the focal point set in Files. See Metafields, Banner image . Typical use. Filters in a column on desktop and a drawer on mobile, 24 products per page with a Load more ","l":"Alignment | Backdrop color | Backdrop intensity | Backdrop size | Background image (mobile) | Badges | Banner image | Banner position (desktop) | Banner position (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Breadcrumbs alignment | Breadcrumbs on this page | Button label | Card content alignment | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Card style | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Element order | Enable filters | Enable sorting | Feature the first product | Filter layout | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Hover effect | Image banner height (desktop) | Image banner height (mobile) | Image fit | Image ratio | Let visitors change the column count (desktop) | Let visitors change the column count (mobile) | Let visitors switch to a list view | Maximum swatches before \"+N\" | Menu | Overlay opacity (image banner) | Padding on the image (desktop) | Padding on the image (mobile) | Pagination | Position | Position on the image (desktop) | Position on the image (mobile) | Product title to price spacing (desktop) | Product title to price spacing (mobile) | Products per page | Quick add | Quick add label | Quick view | Search box from | Second image on hover | Section width | Show collection image | Show collection title | Show color swatches | Show counts on filter values | Show description | Show draggable price range | Show on desktop | Show on mobile | Show results count | Show the product rating | Show vendor | Spacing inside card (desktop) | Spacing inside card (mobile) | Swatch option name | Swatch shape | Swatch size | Text backdrop | Text color on the image | Text shadow | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Values before \"Show more\""},{"t":"Block: Promo tile","p":"Sections / Template sections / Collection","u":"sections.html#s-main-collection-promo-tile","x":"A tile that takes the place of a product card at the position you choose, on the first page of the grid only. This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Button label | Color scheme | Heading | Image | Image (mobile) | Link | Position in the grid | Text | Text alignment | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Search","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-search","x":"Where Part of the search template. The search results page, with the same filters, sorting, pagination and product cards as the collection page. What it searches (products only, or products, articles and pages) is set in Theme settings, Search . Typical use. Filters in a drawer on every device, with infinite scroll. Section background More settings More settings More settings Grid Filters and sorting Product cards Spacing This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Background image (mobile) | Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Element order | Enable filters | Enable sorting | Field placeholder | Filter layout | Gradient style | Grain | Image fit | Image ratio | Pagination | Product title to price spacing (desktop) | Product title to price spacing (mobile) | Quick add | Quick add label | Quick view | Results per page | Search box from | Second image on hover | Section width | Show color swatches | Show counts on filter values | Show draggable price range | Show results count | Show vendor | Spacing inside card (desktop) | Spacing inside card (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Values before \"Show more\""},{"t":"Collections list","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-list-collections","x":"Where Part of the list of collections template. The page that lists your collections ( /collections ): every collection alphabetically, or only the ones you pick, in the order you pick them. Typical use. A curated list of six collections, with the product count on each card. Section background More settings More settings More settings Heading Collections Cards Spacing This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Card title size (desktop) | Card title size (mobile) | Collections per page | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Curated collections (optional) | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Heading | Image fit | Image ratio | Section width | Show heading | Show product count | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Cart","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-cart","x":"Where Part of the cart template. The cart page: the lines beside a summary that follows the scroll, with quantity rules, the order note, the discount code, the free shipping bar, the totals and the accelerated checkout buttons. It works without JavaScript. What it shows is set once for the page and the drawer in Theme settings, Cart ; the section keeps its color scheme, width and background. Gift wrapping appears here when it is on in Theme settings. Typical use. An order note for delivery instructions and the accelerated checkout buttons under the checkout button. Section background More settings More settings More settings This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Background image (mobile) | Color scheme | Gradient style | Grain | Section width"},{"t":"Cart drawer","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-cart-drawer","x":"Where Part of every page. It is listed in the theme editor and cannot be removed or moved. The panel that slides in when a product is added to the cart, or the short notification that replaces it. It has no settings of its own: its type, style, free shipping bar, recommendations, order note, discount code and checkout buttons are set in Theme settings, Cart , shared with the cart page. The free shipping bar only displays progress toward the amount you type. It does not create free shipping or a discount: set the real rule in your admin (Settings, Shipping and delivery, or Discounts) and keep the two amounts the same. Typical use. A floating glass drawer with a free shipping bar at 50 in your currency, three complementary suggestions in a carousel and the order note."},{"t":"Blog","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-blog","x":"Where Part of the blog template. The blog page: article cards with image, date, author, excerpt and tags, an optional row of tag filters, and page numbers. Typical use. Three columns on desktop, one on mobile, with the tag filter row for recipes and news. Section background More settings More settings More settings Layout Cards Metadata Spacing This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Articles per page | Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Card title size (desktop) | Card title size (mobile) | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Excerpt length (words) | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Image fit | Image ratio | Section width | Show author | Show date | Show excerpt | Show featured image | Show tag filter row | Show tags on cards | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Article","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-article","x":"Where Part of the article template. A blog post: featured image, date, author, tags, share buttons, links to the previous and next posts, and comments when the blog allows them, in a reading column whose width and type sizes you set. Typical use. A reading column of about 700 px with the share buttons and the previous and next links. Section background More settings More settings More settings Content Comments Reading column Typography Spacing Breadcrumbs This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Background image (mobile) | Body text size (desktop) | Body text size (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Breadcrumbs alignment | Breadcrumbs on this page | Color scheme | Column width (desktop) | Column width (mobile) | Comments per page | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Section width | Show author | Show date | Show featured image | Show previous / next articles | Show share buttons | Show tags | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Page","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-page","x":"Where Part of the page template. A standard page from your admin (Online Store, Pages) in a reading column, with its title and content. Typical use. Legal pages, shipping information and other text pages. Section background More settings More settings More settings Reading column Typography Spacing This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Background image (mobile) | Body text size (desktop) | Body text size (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Column width (desktop) | Column width (mobile) | Content width | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Page title alignment (desktop) | Page title alignment (mobile) | Section width | Show page title | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"404 page","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-404","x":"Where Part of the 404 template. The page shown when a link is broken: a heading, a message, a button home, an optional search bar and a few products from a collection of your choice. Typical use. A friendly message, the search bar and four best sellers to keep the visitor in the store. Section background More settings More settings More settings Content Search Featured collection Typography Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Collection | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Featured heading | Gradient style | Grain | Header over this section | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Home button label | Message | Products shown | Search button label | Search placeholder | Section width | Show search bar | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Password page","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-password","x":"Where Part of the password template. The page visitors see while your store is password protected, with your logo, the password form and a background. The message above the form is set in Online Store, Preferences. Typical use. A coming soon page before launch. Branding Content Background Typography Spacing","l":"Background image | Color scheme | Extra bottom padding (desktop) | Extra bottom padding (mobile) | Extra top padding (desktop) | Extra top padding (mobile) | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Image overlay opacity | Logo image | Logo width (desktop) | Logo width (mobile) | Password field label | Password placeholder | Section width | Submit button label"},{"t":"Gift card","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-gift-card","x":"Where Part of the gift card template. The page a customer opens from their gift card email, with the card value, the code, a QR code, and buttons to copy the code, print the page and go to the store. Typical use. Your logo on top, on your main color scheme. Section background More settings More settings More settings Branding Content Typography Spacing Three more sections exist in the theme files without appearing in the section list: Quick view, Predictive search and Pickup availability. They have no settings; the theme loads them on demand to fill the quick view modal, the search suggestions and the pickup details. Quick view is configured in Theme settings, Quick view , predictive search in the Header section. Preview versions of Balm also offered a Lifestyle strip section, two photos side by side in one rounded card. It has been removed.","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Code hint | Color scheme | Copy button label | Gradient style | Grain | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Logo image | Print button label | QR code hint | Section width | Shop button label | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Blocks used inside sections","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#blocks","x":"Blocks that several sections accept, and the blocks that build the header mega menus."},{"t":"Theme blocks","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections","u":"sections.html#theme-blocks","x":"General purpose blocks accepted by Image with text, Rich text and the product information column. Stack them in any order to build a content column."},{"t":"Heading","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Theme blocks","u":"sections.html#tb-heading","x":"A heading. Heading level (semantic) sets the level for search engines and screen readers without changing the size.","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Alignment (mobile) | Heading level (semantic) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Text | Typography style"},{"t":"Text","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Theme blocks","u":"sections.html#tb-text","x":"A rich text paragraph, with an optional maximum width.","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Alignment (mobile) | Limit text width | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Max text width | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Text"},{"t":"Button","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Theme blocks","u":"sections.html#tb-button","x":"A link styled as a Solid, Outline or Glass button, or as a text link.","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Alignment (mobile) | Label | Link | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Open in a new tab | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Style"},{"t":"Image","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Theme blocks","u":"sections.html#tb-image","x":"An image with a ratio, a width, an optional height limit and a corner radius.","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Alignment (mobile) | Corner radius | Fit (when a ratio is set) | Image | Limit height | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Max height (desktop) | Max height (mobile) | Ratio | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Spacer","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Theme blocks","u":"sections.html#tb-spacer","x":"Empty space, with its own height on desktop and mobile.","l":"Height (desktop) | Height (mobile)"},{"t":"Liquid","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Theme blocks","u":"sections.html#tb-liquid","x":"Your own Liquid or HTML. See Custom code .","l":"Liquid code"},{"t":"Mega menu blocks","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections","u":"sections.html#mega-menu-blocks","x":"A mega menu is a panel that opens under a top level item of the main menu. Add a Mega menu block to the Header section, type the exact title of that menu item in Linked menu item , then add the blocks below inside it. On phones the panel becomes an accordion in the mobile menu."},{"t":"Mega menu","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-menu","x":"The panel itself: which menu item opens it, its layout, width, background and padding. Layout builds the panel from the sub-links of the linked menu item ( Links and images , Images only or Links only ) or from the blocks you add inside it ( Custom blocks ). With Custom blocks, the blocks sit on one row of the panel and wrap onto a new row when they do not fit, exactly Block spacing (desktop) apart. Each block has a Width (desktop) : Auto (its content), 1/4, 1/3, 1/2, 2/3 or Fill (what the others leave). Horizontal alignment (desktop) and Vertical alignment (desktop) place them when they leave room. Media height (desktop) on Match tallest, the default, gives every block with a picture the height of the tallest one, text under the picture included, so every bottom lines up; Fixed uses the height you set. In the mobile menu the links come first, then the cards (Promo, Image and each card of Image cards), all of the same width and Card ratio (mobile) , laid out by Mobile cards layout : Carousel (one row that scrolls sideways, the next card showing), Grid (two columns) or Stack. Grid Mobile menu Panel dimensions Inner padding Accepts these blocks inside it: Link column, Image, Image ca","l":"Block spacing (desktop) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Card ratio (mobile) | Card spacing (mobile) | Carousel card width (mobile) | Height (desktop) | Horizontal alignment (desktop) | Horizontal padding (desktop) | Horizontal padding (mobile) | Layout | Link columns | Linked menu item | Links width (desktop) | Max width (desktop) | Media height (desktop) | Mobile cards layout | Panel background | Panel width (desktop) | Top padding (desktop) | Vertical alignment (desktop) | Vertical padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Link column","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-column","x":"A list of links. Menu picks one of your menus, the header's main menu when empty. Links shows All links, or Only the links under a Parent link , by default the item the mega menu opens from. Heading defaults to the title of the parent link; in the mobile menu the heading folds the links like an accordion, and without it they show at once. Second and third level links get a Sub-link indent . Group spacing sets the space between the first level links, each with the links under it, and Link spacing the space between the links under them, on desktop and on mobile. Show thumbnails puts the picture of each product and collection link before it, with its size and corner radius; the other links keep its room, so the texts line up. Layout Spacing Typography Thumbnails","l":"Group spacing (desktop) | Group spacing (mobile) | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Heading to links spacing (desktop) | Heading to links spacing (mobile) | Link size (desktop) | Link size (mobile) | Link spacing (desktop) | Link spacing (mobile) | Links | Menu | Parent link | Show heading (desktop) | Show heading (mobile) | Show thumbnails (desktop) | Show thumbnails (mobile) | Sub-link indent (desktop) | Sub-link indent (mobile) | Sub-link size (desktop) | Sub-link size (mobile) | Thumbnail corner radius | Thumbnail size (desktop) | Thumbnail size (mobile) | Thumbnails for | Vertical padding (desktop) | Width (desktop)"},{"t":"Image","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-image","x":"An image with an optional caption, subtitle and link label, under the picture or on it, cropped at its focal point. Nothing shows on the storefront without a picture. Layout Image crop Spacing Caption Typography Mobile","l":"Backdrop color | Backdrop intensity | Backdrop size | Caption | Caption alignment | Caption size (desktop) | Caption size (mobile) | Caption top spacing (desktop) | Corner radius | Crop | Custom corner radius | Heading case (desktop) | Heading case (mobile) | Heading weight (desktop) | Heading weight (mobile) | Image | Image / caption gap (mobile) | Image alignment (desktop) | Image height (desktop) | Image ratio (desktop) | Image width (desktop) | Link | Link label | Padding on the image (desktop) | Padding on the image (mobile) | Position on the image (desktop) | Position on the image (mobile) | Show in the mobile menu | Subtitle | Subtitle size (desktop) | Subtitle size (mobile) | Text backdrop | Text color on the image | Text position | Text shadow | Vertical padding (desktop) | Width (desktop)"},{"t":"Image cards","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-cards","x":"A row of up to four picture cards. Image source set to Automatic shows the picture of what each sub-link of the linked menu item points to: a collection or a product (with its price), a blog post, or a page through its custom.image metafield (see Metafields, Page image ). Custom cards shows the Image card blocks you add inside it. Every picture is cropped at its focal point, in the Image ratio (desktop) you pick (Original, Square, three portrait and three landscape ratios, or a fixed height), with the media corner radius of Theme settings or your own, and a Hover effect (Zoom, Fade or None). The text sits below the picture or on it: on the picture, place it in one of nine positions per device and add a Text backdrop (Soft gradient or Soft glow) only where the text is, so it reads on any photo. Images Text Typography Mobile menu Accepts these blocks inside it: Image card.","l":"Backdrop color | Backdrop intensity | Backdrop size | Button style | Card width (desktop) | Corner radius | Custom corner radius | Heading case (desktop) | Heading case (mobile) | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Heading weight (desktop) | Heading weight (mobile) | Hover effect | Image height (desktop) | Image ratio (desktop) | Image source | Number of cards | Padding on the image (desktop) | Padding on the image (mobile) | Position on the image (desktop) | Position on the image (mobile) | Show cards in the mobile menu | Space between image and heading | Spacing (desktop) | Subtitle size (desktop) | Subtitle size (mobile) | Text alignment | Text backdrop | Text color on the image | Text position | Text shadow | Width (desktop)"},{"t":"Image card","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-card","x":"One card of an Image cards block set to Custom cards: an image, a heading, a subtitle, a link and an optional button label.","l":"Button label | Heading | Image | Link | Subtitle"},{"t":"Products","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-products","x":"Two to four products as mini cards with image, title and price. With Show product tagline on in the Header section, each card also shows the product's custom.tagline metafield. Grid Thumbnails Content Mobile","l":"Card alignment | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Grid columns (desktop) | Grid columns (mobile) | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Heading top spacing (desktop) | Heading top spacing (mobile) | Price size (desktop) | Price size (mobile) | Products | Show (mobile) | Show price | Thumbnail crop | Thumbnail ratio | Vertical padding (desktop) | Vertical padding (mobile) | Width (desktop)"},{"t":"Promo","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-promo","x":"An image tile with a heading, a short text and a link. Image Layout Text Typography Spacing Mobile","l":"Alignment | Backdrop color | Backdrop intensity | Backdrop size | Heading | Heading case (desktop) | Heading case (mobile) | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Heading top spacing (desktop) | Heading top spacing (mobile) | Heading weight (desktop) | Heading weight (mobile) | Image | Image fit | Image ratio | Link | Link label | Padding on the image (desktop) | Padding on the image (mobile) | Position on the image (desktop) | Position on the image (mobile) | Show (mobile) | Text | Text backdrop | Text color on the image | Text position | Text shadow | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Text top spacing (desktop) | Text top spacing (mobile) | Tile max width (desktop) | Vertical padding (desktop) | Width (desktop)"},{"t":"Banner","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-banner","x":"A wide banner with a background image, a heading, a short text and a button or link. Dimensions Background image Legibility overlay Content Typography Button Mobile","l":"Background crop | Background image | Button label | Button size (desktop) | Button size (mobile) | Button style | Button top spacing (desktop) | Button top spacing (mobile) | Content horizontal alignment | Content vertical alignment | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Horizontal padding (desktop) | Horizontal padding (mobile) | Link | Max text width (desktop) | Max text width (mobile) | Minimum height (desktop) | Minimum height (mobile) | Overlay color | Overlay opacity | Overlay style | Ratio (optional) | Short text | Show (mobile) | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Text top spacing (desktop) | Text top spacing (mobile) | Vertical padding (desktop) | Vertical padding (mobile) | Width (desktop)"},{"t":"Product page blocks","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html","x":"Balm ships one product page, and every product uses it. You shape it from the theme editor, and you can let each product carry its own colors and texts through metafields, so you never need a second template."},{"t":"How the page is built","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#how-it-is-built","x":"The Product section is a two column layout: the media gallery on one side, a column of blocks on the other. Add, remove and reorder the blocks in the theme editor: Online Store, Themes, Customize , then pick Products in the page menu at the top. The section also accepts app blocks , so any app that offers a block (reviews, subscriptions, bundles) drops straight into the column, and the general theme blocks (Heading, Button, Spacer and the others). The template, templates/product.json , starts with this stack: Blocks marked shown only when render nothing on products that do not need them, so the page stays short even though the stack is long. The template carries no example text: a block whose text is empty shows nothing on the storefront, not even its spacing, and a dimmed example in the theme editor. Below the section, the template places, as on the demo store, a Slideshow , the Sticky add to cart bar, Key ingredients , a Routine , Before and after , Compare products , an FAQ , Testimonials and Product recommendations . Fill them, or remove the ones you do not need. Add an Icon list block for reassurance claims under the buy buttons. The Product section is the main section of the "},{"t":"Buy button styles","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#buy-button-styles","x":"The Style setting of the Buy buttons block offers five looks. Each keeps its own Corner radius , Font weight and Letter case settings, so you can land anywhere between them. Welding joins the buy button to the Packs menu variant picker so the two read as one shape. It needs the Signature pill style, because the seam depends on its square corner. Turn on Weld to the buy button in the Variant picker block and Weld to the packs menu in the Buy buttons block."},{"t":"About the Glass style","p":"Product page blocks / Buy button styles","u":"product-page.html#glass-style","x":"Glass takes its recipe from Theme settings, Glass effect : one tint, one opacity, one blur and one border opacity, shared by every glass surface. Change it once and the buy button, the upsell buttons, the popup trigger, the newsletter card and the cart panel move together. The label keeps the text color of the section's color scheme. Balm measures the contrast between that color and the frosted surface, and only when it falls below 3:1 (the WCAG floor for large text) does it switch the label to black or white, whichever reads better. Over a background image or a gradient the backdrop changes from pixel to pixel, so the theme leaves your scheme color alone there: check the contrast yourself. Glass is available on the buy button, on the Product upsell buttons ( Button style , separate from the card style) and on the Popup trigger."},{"t":"Variant picker styles","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#variant-picker-styles","x":"Swatch styles fall back to a text pill for option values with no swatch saved. Unavailable option values grays out or hides combinations that cannot be bought. Products that belong to a combined listing switch to the sibling product when a shopper picks one of its values: see Combined listings ."},{"t":"Ready-made backgrounds","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#backgrounds","x":"The Product section can paint its own background. The setting is Background mode , at the top of the section settings, with six modes: None (use the color scheme) , Solid color , Gradient (two colors) , Image , Radial halo and Product gradient (metafields) . The template default is None (use the color scheme) . The three combinations below are ready to copy, and the fourth, Product gradient , gives every product its own colors with nothing to connect."},{"t":"A. Soft gradient","p":"Product page blocks / Ready-made backgrounds","u":"product-page.html#bg-soft-gradient","x":"A near white wash that lifts the packshot without coloring it. These gradient colors are already typed into the template, so switching the mode is all it takes."},{"t":"B. Warm paper","p":"Product page blocks / Ready-made backgrounds","u":"product-page.html#bg-warm-paper","x":"A single flat color. The calmest option, and the easiest to connect to a metafield so each product carries its own shade."},{"t":"C. Radial halo","p":"Product page blocks / Ready-made backgrounds","u":"product-page.html#bg-radial-halo","x":"A dark halo anchored in one corner over a light base. The most dramatic of the three; use it when the packshot is cut out on a transparent background. To give every product its own background color, connect these colors to product metafields: the step by step guide is on Metafields . For a gradient, the Product gradient mode below does it without any connection."},{"t":"D. Product gradient","p":"Product page blocks / Ready-made backgrounds","u":"product-page.html#bg-product-gradient","x":"Each product paints its own gradient from two Color metafields, read directly: custom.background_color for the start and custom.background_color_end for the end. There is nothing to connect in the theme editor: create the two definitions once (see Metafields ), fill them on each product, and choose the mode. Both colors filled : the gradient runs from the first to the second, in the direction set. One color filled : the section is that one color. Neither : the background of the section's color scheme, as in None. Fallback background color plays no part in this mode. The Sticky add to cart bar takes the end color as its accent, as in the Gradient mode. The Products showcase spotlights read the same two metafields, and Featured set the first one, so a product keeps its colors from the home page to its own page."},{"t":"Extend the gradient under the header","p":"Product page blocks / Ready-made backgrounds","u":"product-page.html#bg-under-header","x":"Over a hero, a transparent header lets the image run to the top of the screen. The product page can do the same with its gradient. The setting is Extend the background under the header , shown in the Product gradient mode, off by default. It needs two conditions: the Header section has Header behavior on Transparent at top or Adaptive ; the Product section is the first section of the product template, as it is in the templates Balm ships. The gradient then starts at the top of the screen, under the header and under a Floating or Glass announcement bar. A Solid announcement bar in full width keeps its place above it. The header is transparent at rest and takes its card on scroll, as it does over a hero. The product content and the breadcrumbs stay clear of it: the section adds the height of the header to its top padding. Without either condition, the setting has no effect. There is nothing to choose for the header's colors: it reads each product's gradient where it lies under the header. Over a dark gradient it takes its Colors over dark backgrounds and its Logo for dark backgrounds , over a light one it keeps its own color scheme and logo, product by product. See Automatic header c"},{"t":"Sticky columns","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#sticky-columns","x":"Sticky columns (desktop) , in the Layout group of the Product section, is on by default. From 768 px wide, the shorter of the two columns, the gallery or the product information, stays in view under the header while the other one scrolls, and the end of the section releases it. A column taller than the screen scrolls until its bottom shows, then holds. On phones the columns stack and nothing is sticky. The setting was named Sticky product info in preview versions, when only the information column could hold."},{"t":"Text behind cutout images","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#text-behind-cutouts","x":"The Product section can print a large decorative text behind the cutout images of its gallery: PNG and WebP images, whose transparent areas let the text show through. JPG images, videos and 3D models stay as they are. The theme knows a cutout by its file format only, so a PNG without transparency also gets the text, hidden behind its opaque pixels. The settings are in the Text behind cutouts group, off by default. Check Show on desktop , Show on mobile , or both. Desktop starts at 768 px wide. Choose the Text : Product title (the default), Product tagline (custom.tagline) , read from the product's metafield, or Custom text , the same on every product. A product whose tagline is empty shows no text. Set Apply to : First image only (the default) shows the text when the first media of the gallery is a PNG or WebP image; All cutout images puts it behind every one. Style it: Font (heading or body font), Font weight (Bold by default), Text case (UPPERCASE by default), Text size (160 px on desktop, 80 px on mobile) and the Vertical position and Horizontal position of each device (centered by default). Pick the Text color : Color scheme text , Gradient end color (custom.background_color_en"},{"t":"The accelerated checkout buttons","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#accelerated-checkout","x":"With Dynamic checkout buttons on, the wallet buttons (Shop Pay, PayPal, Google Pay, Apple Pay) show under Add to cart. Which ones appear depends on the payment methods your store has enabled and on the visitor's browser, so the row differs from one shopper to the next. The row follows the selected variant: it is hidden while that variant is sold out or unavailable and comes back as soon as a variant that can be bought is chosen. A pre-order variant can be bought, so it keeps the row. Quick view and the sticky add to cart bar have no accelerated checkout buttons. These buttons are drawn by Shopify, inside an element no theme and no app can style directly. Shopify exposes a short list of settings instead, and Balm sets all of them from your Add to cart button: No theme can change the brand color of each button, its logo, its label or its font: Shop Pay stays purple and PayPal yellow on every Shopify store. Because Shopify caps the wallet height at 55 px, a Button height above 55 makes Add to cart taller than the wallet row; keep it at 55 or below if you want the two to match. The cart drawer and the cart page get the same treatment."},{"t":"Product section settings","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#product-section-settings","x":"Settings of the Product section itself: background (with the product metafields they connect to, and the Product gradient that reads them directly), product vignette, bottom curve, layout ( sticky columns and one collapsible row open at a time), gallery, badges on media, packshot captions, text behind cutouts , video and 3D, spacing and breadcrumbs. The spacing between collapsible rows is set on each row. Select the section in the editor, above its blocks, to see them. Section background Solid color settings Gradient settings Image settings Radial halo settings Background illustration Background · Bottom curve Layout Media Gallery layout Packshot captions Text behind cutouts Video and 3D Spacing Breadcrumbs","l":"Animate the aurora slowly | Animation | Apply to | Autoplay videos | Background color | Background illustration | Background image | Background mode | Badges on media | Base color | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Breadcrumbs alignment | Breadcrumbs on this page | Caption alignment | Caption case | Caption color | Caption size (desktop) | Caption size (mobile) | Caption source | Caption weight | Carousel position indicator | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Curve color | Curve height (desktop) | Curve height (mobile) | Custom color | Custom text | Desktop layout | Extend the background under the header | Fallback background color | Fit (when a ratio is set) | Flip curve | Font | Font weight | Gallery arrows | Gallery width (desktop) | Gap between columns (desktop) | Gap between media (desktop) | Gap between media (mobile) | Glow horizontal position on desktop | Glow horizontal position on mobile | Glow size on desktop | Glow size on mobile | Glow vertical position on desktop | Glow vertical position on mobile | Gradient direction | Gradient end | Gradient start | Gradient style | Grain | Halo color | Halo position | Halo size (desktop) | Halo size (mobile) | Halo solid area | Horizontal position (desktop) | Horizontal position (mobile) | Illustration horizontal alignment (desktop) | Illustration horizontal alignment (mobile) | Illustration horizontal offset (desktop) | Illustration horizontal offset (mobile) | Illustration opacity | Illustration vertical alignment (desktop) | Illustration vertical alignment (mobile) | Illustration vertical offset (desktop) | Illustration vertical offset (mobile) | Illustration width (desktop) | Illustration width (mobile) | Letter spacing | Line height | Lines | Loop videos | Maximum zoom level | Media controls style | Media corner radius | Media ratio (desktop) | Media ratio (mobile) | Metafield | Mobile layout | Mute videos | Next-slide peek (mobile) | One collapsible row open at a time | Outline thickness | Overlay color | Overlay opacity | Section width | Shape | Shape image | Show background illustration | Show bottom curve | Show captions | Show on desktop | Show on mobile | Show the AR button on 3D models | Show thumbnails | Show video controls | Sizing | Space above the caption | Sticky columns (desktop) | Style | Text | Text case | Text color | Text colors | Text opacity | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Text style | Thumbnail size | Thumbnail size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Vertical position (desktop) | Vertical position (mobile) | Viewer height (desktop) | Zone | Zoom image"},{"t":"Blocks","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#blocks","x":"Every block of the product information column, with the name the block picker shows. Settings that can be connected to a product metafield say so in their notes, with the exact definition to create; the full list is on Metafields . Product title Vendor Price SKU Rating Text Variant picker Volume pricing Purchase options Gift card recipient Buy buttons Stock status Back in stock Pickup availability Payment icons Product upsell Complementary products Description Collapsible row Popup Specifications Specification Icon list Icon item Image Badge Spinning badge Share Product navigation Liquid"},{"t":"Product title","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-title","x":"The product title, the main heading of the page. Keep one Title block on H1; any extra title block should use a subheading level.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Heading level | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Typography style"},{"t":"Vendor","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-vendor","x":"The brand or maker name, from the product admin page.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Price","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-price","x":"The price, the compare-at price, the unit price and an optional taxes and shipping note. It follows the selected variant.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Show compare-at price | Show unit price | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Taxes and shipping note | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"SKU","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-sku","x":"The SKU of the selected variant, with an optional prefix.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Prefix | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Rating","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-rating","x":"Stars, the numeric value and the review count, read from the standard reviews.rating and reviews.rating_count metafields that review apps fill. It renders nothing until an app fills them. Spacing","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Show the numeric value | Show the review count | Star color | Star size (desktop) | Star size (mobile) | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Text","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-text","x":"A free rich text paragraph, the same on every product, or with Source set to Tagline , the product's own custom.tagline metafield, read directly. Empty, it shows nothing on the storefront.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Source | Text | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Variant picker","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-variant-picker","x":"The options the customer chooses from, in one of six styles (see Variant picker styles ). It handles products with many variants, combined listings and unavailable combinations. Swatches Unavailable combinations Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Show a price per option | Show option names | Show the selected value next to the option name | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Style | Swatch shape | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Unavailable option values | Weld to the buy button"},{"t":"Volume pricing","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-volume-pricing","x":"Quantity price breaks, as a table or a list. It renders nothing when the variant has none. Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Heading | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Show heading | Show the price for the chosen quantity | Style | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Purchase options","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-selling-plans","x":"One-time purchase and subscription options from your subscription app, with the plan names, descriptions and savings. It renders nothing unless the product has a selling plan. Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Heading | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | One-time purchase label | Show the plan description | Show the plan group name | Show the savings | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Gift card recipient","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-gift-card-recipient","x":"Lets the buyer send a gift card to someone else, with a name, an email, a message and a send date. It only renders on gift card products. Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Toggle label | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Buy buttons","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-buy-buttons","x":"The quantity selector, Add to cart, the accelerated checkout buttons and the Shop Pay Installments banner. The quantity selector is the only one of the product page: Quantity selector (desktop) and Quantity selector (mobile) place it Above the buttons (the default), Inline with Add to cart, or Hidden, with its style, size and label; it follows the quantity rules of each variant and volume pricing. Preview versions of Balm had a separate Quantity block; it has been removed. The accelerated checkout buttons (Buy it now and the wallets) are hidden while the selected variant is sold out and come back with a variant in stock; a pre-order variant can be bought, so it keeps them, and its button reads Pre-order. See Buy button styles , accelerated checkout and Pre-order . Quantity selector","l":"Add to cart label | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button height | Button size | Corner radius | Corner style | Dynamic checkout buttons | Font weight | Full width Add to cart | Letter case | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Quantity selector (desktop) | Quantity selector (mobile) | Quantity selector size | Quantity selector style | Shop Pay Installments banner | Show quantity label | Sold out label | Style | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Unavailable label | Weld to the packs menu"},{"t":"Stock status","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-inventory","x":"In stock, low stock or out of stock for the selected variant, with a colored dot and an optional exact quantity. Low stock only applies when inventory is tracked and the variant stops selling at zero. Spacing","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Dot size | In-stock color | In-stock label | Low stock threshold | Low-stock color | Low-stock label | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Out-of-stock color | Out-of-stock label | Show the exact quantity | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Back in stock","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-notify-me","x":"A back in stock form, shown only while the selected variant is sold out. Requests arrive as contact form messages, at the store address set in Settings, Notifications, and name the exact variant; no app is needed. Style Spacing","l":"Ask for a name | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Button style | Email placeholder | Heading | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Show heading | Subtext | Success message | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Pickup availability","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-pickup","x":"Local pickup availability for the selected variant, and a button that opens the list of locations. It renders nothing unless a location has pickup enabled. Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Payment icons","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-payment-icons","x":"A reassurance line and the icons of the payment methods enabled in your store (Settings, Payments). A theme cannot add or reorder these icons; to show another badge, upload it as the block image. Spacing","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Icon size | Image | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Show the reassurance line | Space between icons | Text | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Product upsell","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-upsell","x":"Frequently bought together: products to buy alongside this one, from Shopify recommendations or your own selection. Bundle (tick boxes, one total) adds every ticked product in one action; Simple list (add one by one) gives each product its own button. The block takes the look of the product cards. Card style is Card (filled with the secondary background of the color scheme), Bordered (a fine outline, the default) or Plain (no box), with the corner radius of the cards set in Theme settings, Corner style . Thumbnails are square and never cropped, with their own size on desktop (72 px) and on mobile (64 px). In the bundle list, each row shows a checkbox, the thumbnail, the title and the price, with a quiet variant menu underneath for products with options, and a thin rule between rows; a Total line and a full width button close the block. Button style is Solid or Glass, separate from the card style. Source Layout Content Style Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Bundle button label | Button style | Card style | Card title size (desktop) | Card title size (mobile) | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Heading | Layout | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Number of products | Presentation | Products | Products come from | Products with several variants | Recommendation intent | Row button label | Show compare-at price | Show heading | Show price | Show product image | Space between products (desktop) | Space between products (mobile) | Thumbnail background | Thumbnail size (desktop) | Thumbnail size (mobile) | Tick every product by default | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Complementary products","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-complementary","x":"A small grid of product cards: complementary products from Shopify recommendations, curated in the Search & Discovery app, or your own selection, which can be connected to a product list metafield. Spacing","l":"Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Card title size (desktop) | Card title size (mobile) | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Heading | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Number of products | Products | Products come from | Show heading | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Description","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-description","x":"The product description from the product admin page.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Collapsible row","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-collapsible-row","x":"An accordion row whose content is rich text, which can be connected to a metafield, or a page, to share one policy page across every product. A row without heading or content shows nothing on the storefront. Style is Lines (the default: heading on the left, icon on the right, thin rules and no frame), Boxed (a framed row) or Filled (the secondary background of the color scheme). Open and close icon is a Chevron that turns over, or a Plus that becomes a minus. The heading has its alignment, its size on desktop and on mobile, and its weight; Inner padding and Space between rows (desktop) and (mobile) are set per device too. Space between rows only shows with Boxed and Filled: stacked Lines rows share one rule between them. Set the style on each row, and give the rows of one stack the same values. Open by default opens the row when the page loads: check it on the first row to show its content at once. To let only one row stay open, turn on One collapsible row open at a time in the Product section. Rows open with a short animation where the browser supports it, and at once for visitors who ask for reduced motion. Style Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Content | Content comes from | Heading | Heading alignment | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Heading weight | Icon | Icon size | Inner padding (desktop) | Inner padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Open and close icon | Open by default | Page | Space between rows (desktop) | Space between rows (mobile) | Style | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Popup","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-popup","x":"A link or button that opens a dialog with rich text or a page. The Under-title link style sits right below the product title. Without content, it shows nothing on the storefront. Modal content Spacing","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Content | Content comes from | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Modal heading | Modal width | Page | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Trigger label | Trigger style"},{"t":"Specifications","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-specs","x":"A label and value table built from Specification blocks, with lines, dots or zebra stripes between rows. Style Typography Spacing Accepts these blocks inside it: Specification.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Gap between columns (desktop) | Gap between columns (mobile) | Heading | Label size (desktop) | Label size (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Row padding (desktop) | Row padding (mobile) | Row separator | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Value alignment | Value size (desktop) | Value size (mobile)"},{"t":"Specification","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-spec-row","x":"One row of the Specifications block. Both the label and the value can be connected to product metafields.","l":"Label | Value"},{"t":"Icon list","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-icon-list","x":"Reassurance claims built from Icon item blocks, stacked, side by side, or on one row with a button. Icon stroke (Light, Regular, Medium or Bold) sets the line weight of the built in icons; your own images keep theirs. Heading weight and Body text weight set the weight of the two lines of text, and Alignment (desktop) and Alignment (mobile) place each claim, icon and text together, on the left, in the center or on the right of its column. Icon sizes, text sizes and gaps have a desktop and a mobile value. Icon and text gap (desktop) and (mobile) set the space the eye sees between each icon and its text, from the bottom of the icon to the top of the capitals: at 0 the letters touch the icon. Layout Typography Spacing Accepts these blocks inside it: Icon item.","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Alignment (mobile) | Body text size (desktop) | Body text size (mobile) | Body text weight | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Button link | Button style | Button text size (desktop) | Button text size (mobile) | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Gap between items (desktop) | Gap between items (mobile) | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Heading weight | Icon and text gap (desktop) | Icon and text gap (mobile) | Icon size (desktop) | Icon size (mobile) | Icon stroke | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Space before the button | Style | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Icon item","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-icon-item","x":"One claim of the Icon list: a built in glyph or your own image, a Heading and a Text . Heading and Text are rich text fields: press Enter for a new line, or connect a product metafield of type Single line text or Multi-line text with the dynamic source icon, each line of a Multi-line text on its own line. The Icon image connects to a File metafield the same way, so each product shows its own claims. See Icon metafields . An item with neither heading nor text stays hidden on the storefront.","l":"Earlier heading | Earlier text | Glyph | Heading | Icon image | Icon type | Text"},{"t":"Image","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-image","x":"An image inside the information column, with an optional caption. Connect it to a metafield to show a different image per product. Caption Spacing","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Aspect ratio | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Caption | Corner radius | Fit (when a ratio is set) | Image | Image width (desktop) | Image width (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Space above the caption | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Badge","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-badge","x":"Automatic (Sale, Sold out, New, Custom) , the default, shows the same badges as the product cards, styled in Theme settings, Product badges, and nothing when none applies. Sale and Sold out follow the selected variant, and the Custom badge wears the product's own colors when its custom.badge_color or custom.badge_text_color metafield is filled (see badge colors ). Image places your own artwork in a corner of the product area. Spacing","l":"Badge type | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Edge offset (desktop) | Edge offset (mobile) | Image | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Position | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Spinning badge","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-spin-badge","x":"The product's custom.badge_label text turning around a ring. The ring has no text field of its own: each product says its own words through the metafield, and a product without it shows no ring. In the theme editor, an example stands in. Position (desktop) and Position (mobile) place the ring on a corner of the gallery (top left, top right, bottom left, bottom right) or Next to the title , on the title's row. Desktop starts at 768 px wide, and the ring moves when the screen crosses that width. Next to the title needs a Title block; without one, the ring shows where the Spinning badge block sits. Place behind the product slides the ring behind the product image, which cuts into it, on the gallery positions only. Size and offsets are set per device. The rotation stops for visitors who ask for reduced motion. Motion Position","l":"Background color | Direction | Horizontal offset (desktop) | Horizontal offset (mobile) | One full turn | Place behind the product | Position (desktop) | Position (mobile) | Repeats | Separator | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Text color | Text size | Vertical offset (desktop) | Vertical offset (mobile)"},{"t":"Share","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-share","x":"Share links for X, Facebook and Pinterest, and a copy link button. Spacing","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Label | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Show Facebook | Show Pinterest | Show X | Show copy link | Show label | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Product navigation","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-nav","x":"Links to the previous and next product of a collection (the product's first collection by default). Only the first 50 products of the collection are read. Layout Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Collection | Gap | Horizontal alignment | Loop around | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Next label | Previous label | Show product names | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Style | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Liquid","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-liquid","x":"Your own Liquid or HTML, or the insertion code of an app that has no app block. See Custom code .","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Liquid code | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"When one product needs a different layout","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#second-template","x":"Metafields let one template carry different colors, texts and images per product. Some settings cannot be connected to a metafield: sliders, checkboxes, dropdowns, the color scheme and Liquid code. When a product needs a different value for one of those, create a second template: in the theme editor, open Products in the page menu, choose Create template , base it on the default product template, then assign it to the product from its admin page, under Theme template ."},{"t":"Products that used an older template","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#older-templates","x":"Early versions of Balm shipped extra product templates. They have been folded into the default one. A product still assigned to one of them falls back to the default product template and renders normally. To clear the setting, open the product in the admin and choose Default product under Theme template ."},{"t":"Features","p":"Features","u":"features.html","x":"The features that span several sections or the whole store: what they do, where to turn them on and what to know before you rely on them."},{"t":"Quick view","p":"Features","u":"features.html#quick-view","x":"Quick view opens a product in a modal from its card, so shoppers choose a variant and add to cart without leaving the page. The modal shows the gallery with thumbnails, the price with its badges and unit price, the rating, the same variant picker as the product page (swatches included), quantity rules, purchase options, the add to cart button, pickup availability, a short description and a link to the full product page. Adding to cart opens the cart drawer."},{"t":"Turn it on","p":"Features / Quick view","u":"features.html#quick-view-on","x":"Open a section that shows product cards: Collection, Featured collection, Search, Recently viewed or Lookbook. Set Quick view to Show on hover or Always show . On touch screens the button is always visible. In Theme settings, Quick view , choose what the modal shows and its card style: Solid, Tinted glass or Glass. Short description metafield takes the namespace and key of a product metafield, for example custom.short_description ; products without it show the first paragraph of their description, cut to Description length . Preload on hover loads the product when the pointer rests on its card so the modal opens at once, at the cost of more data. Without JavaScript the button simply opens the product page. Quick view is separate from Quick add , the setting that puts an add to cart button on the card itself: Off, Single-variant products, or All products (which opens an option picker for products with variants)."},{"t":"Product badges","p":"Features","u":"features.html#product-badges","x":"Four badges can appear on product cards, in quick view, in Compare products and on the product page. Every one of them states a fact of the product: nothing shows a text typed once for all products. Their position, shape and colors are set once in Theme settings, Product badges .","l":"Custom | New | Sale | Sold out"},{"t":"Set up the Custom badge","p":"Features / Product badges","u":"features.html#custom-badge","x":"Create the custom.badge_label definition once, as described in Metafields, Badge label . Fill it on the products that need a badge, for example Limited edition or Vegan . Leave it empty on the others. That is all: the cards, quick view, Compare products and the product page read the metafield directly. There is no key to type and nothing to connect in the theme editor."},{"t":"Give one product its own badge colors","p":"Features / Product badges","u":"features.html#custom-badge-colors","x":"The Custom badge wears the Custom background and Custom text colors of Theme settings. To color it differently on one product, for example green on a vegan product, create two optional product metafields of type Color : custom.badge_color for the background and custom.badge_text_color for the text (see Metafields, Badge colors ). They change the Custom badge of that product only, everywhere it shows. Sale, Sold out and New keep the colors of Theme settings. Both filled : the badge takes both colors as they are. Background only : the text is picked for you. It takes the text color or the background color of Scheme 1, your main color scheme, whichever contrasts more with the badge. If even that one stays below a contrast of 4.5:1, which happens on mid tones, the text turns pure black or pure white, one of which always reaches it. Text only : the text color sits on the Custom background of Theme settings. Check that the two contrast enough. Neither : the colors of Theme settings, as on every other product."},{"t":"Badges on the product page","p":"Features / Product badges","u":"features.html#badges-product-page","x":"Badges on media , in the Product section settings, shows the badges in the corner of the gallery: Off (the default) or Automatic , the same Sale, Sold out, New and Custom badges as the cards. The Badge block, in the information column, draws the same badges in a row when its Badge type is Automatic (Sale, Sold out, New, Custom) , the default. Its other type, Image , places your own artwork in a corner of the product area. The Spinning badge block turns the custom.badge_label text around a ring, on a corner of the gallery or next to the title, with its own position and size on desktop and on mobile. It has no text field of its own: a product without the metafield shows no ring. See Spinning badge . On the product page, Sale and Sold out follow the selected variant: choosing a variant without a compare-at price removes Sale, choosing a sold out one shows Sold out. When no badge applies, nothing is drawn and no space is left."},{"t":"Choose the badges of each section","p":"Features / Product badges","u":"features.html#badges-per-section","x":"Every section that shows product cards has its own Badges setting: Collection, Search, Featured collection, Product recommendations, Recently viewed, Lookbook, the 404 page, Compare products, the Product tile of Bento and the Complementary products block of the product page. All , the default: every badge that applies. Automatic only : Sale, Sold out and New, as set in Theme settings, Product badges. Custom only : only the product's custom.badge_label metafield. None : no badge in that section. For example, keep All on the collection pages and choose Custom only in Featured collection on the home page, so it shows your Limited edition badges without the Sale ones."},{"t":"Page loader","p":"Features","u":"features.html#page-loader","x":"An optional loading screen shown while pages open, with your logo, a progress bar or a spinner, and an exit animation. Turn it on in Theme settings, Loader , under Page loader : First visit only (recommended) shows it once per visit. Every page shows it on each page view. It can lower speed scores, because the page stays covered while it loads. Layout combines the logo with a progress bar or a spinner, or shows the bar alone. With a progress bar, Bar ends (Square or Rounded, which rounds the track and the fill), Bar thickness (1 to 6 px) and Bar animation set its look: None moves the fill in steps, Smooth fills it continuously, Shimmer adds a gleam in the background color that crosses the filled part in a loop. The logo is the Logo image you pick here, or else the header logo, then the brand logo from your Shopify settings, then the store name. Background is Solid or Glass, on the Color scheme you choose. The Exit animation (Fade, Slide up, Split, Zoom, Circle reveal) plays when the page is ready, never before the Minimum display time and never after the Maximum display time . Page transitions plays the exit in reverse when a visitor follows a link to another page of the store. To "},{"t":"Age verifier","p":"Features","u":"features.html#age-verifier","x":"A modal that asks visitors to confirm their age before they browse the store. It shows on every page of the online store, never at checkout, and waits for the page loader to leave first. In Theme settings, Age verifier , check Enable the age verifier . Set the Minimum age . Write [age] in the texts to print it. Fields left empty use the translated storefront text. Choose what happens when the visitor declines: Show a message or Redirect to a link . Set Remember the answer for : the number of days before the same browser is asked again. 0 asks on every visit. Style it with a background image, a color scheme and a card style. Check Preview in the theme editor to see it while you edit; answers are not remembered while previewing. Raising the minimum age asks every visitor again. A decline is never remembered. The age verifier is a self-declaration, not an identity check: make sure it meets the rules that apply to your products in the countries you sell to."},{"t":"Gift wrapping","p":"Features","u":"features.html#gift-wrapping","x":"Adds a gift wrapping checkbox, and an optional gift message, to the cart drawer and the cart page. Checking the box adds your wrapping product to the cart in quantity 1 and records the cart attribute Gift wrapping: Yes . The message is saved as the cart attribute Gift message . Both appear on the order in your admin. Create a product for the wrapping, for example Gift wrapping , with the price the buyer pays and an image. Make it available on the Online Store sales channel, and keep it out of your collections. In Theme settings, Gift wrapping , check Offer gift wrapping and pick it as the Wrapping product . The option only shows once an available product is chosen. Adjust the Checkbox label , the help text, the gift message and its maximum length, and where it shows: cart drawer, cart page or both. The wrapping line stays at quantity 1, and a cart that holds only the wrapping is emptied, so nobody checks out with the wrapping alone."},{"t":"Lookbook","p":"Features","u":"features.html#lookbook","x":"The Lookbook section turns a photo into a shop: each point on the image opens the product card, with its quick add. On a phone a tap opens the same content as a sheet from the bottom of the screen. Add a Lookbook section and choose an image, plus an optional mobile image. Add one Hotspot block per product and pick the product. A hotspot can carry a text and a link instead. Place each hotspot with Horizontal position and Vertical position , in percent of the image: 0% is the left or top edge, 100% the right or bottom edge. Desktop and mobile positions are separate. For a shoppable list, set Layout to Image with product list : the products line up beside the image, and hovering a card lights its hotspot."},{"t":"Compare products","p":"Features","u":"features.html#compare-products","x":"The Compare products section sets up to five products side by side. Built in rows show the image, the badges, the price, the availability, the vendor and the rating. Each row you add reads one fact on every compared product: a metafield of your choice, or the vendor, product type, tags, SKU, barcode, weight or unit price. Create one product metafield definition per fact you want to compare, in Settings, Custom data, Products. For example Texture and Skin type (Single line text), Fragrance free (True or false). Fill the values on each product. Add the section, pick the products, then add one Row block per fact. Keep Source on Metafield and type the metafield's name in Metafield , for example Skin type , or its key, custom.skin_type . Type a Label for the left column, or leave it empty to use the name of the source. Each value is drawn by its type: a check mark or a cross for true or false, a number followed by the row's Unit , a list as a sentence, a color with its swatch. A product without a value shows a hyphen. Highlight differences marks the rows where products differ. Mobile layout shows one card per product on a phone, or the table with the labels in place while the products s"},{"t":"Recently viewed","p":"Features","u":"features.html#recently-viewed","x":"The product page records each product a visitor opens, in that visitor's own browser. The Recently viewed section reads that list and shows the products, newest first. Nothing is sent to a server and no app or account is needed. The section takes no space until the visitor has a history; in the theme editor it shows example cards instead. Add it to the product template, below Product recommendations, with Exclude the current product on, or to the cart, collection or home page. Maximum products caps the list."},{"t":"Pagination","p":"Features","u":"features.html#pagination","x":"The Collection and Search sections have a Pagination setting with three modes: Page numbers : classic numbered pages. Load more button : the next page is added under the grid when the shopper asks for it. Infinite scroll : the next page is added as the shopper reaches the end of the grid. After three pages a Load more button takes over, so the footer stays reachable. Load more and infinite scroll show a Showing X of Y counter. The number of products per page is set with Products per page on collections and Results per page on search. The blog, the list of collections and blog post comments use page numbers, with their own per page setting. Promo tiles appear on the first page only."},{"t":"Translations","p":"Features","u":"features.html#translations","x":"Balm ships in five languages: English, French, German, Italian and Spanish. That covers every storefront text of the theme (buttons, cart, forms, filters, accessibility labels) and the theme editor itself, which follows the language of your admin. Add and publish your languages in Settings, Languages . The theme's own texts switch automatically. Translate the content you typed in the editor (headings, paragraphs, button labels) with Shopify's free Translate & Adapt app. Leave the text settings marked Leave empty to use the translated default empty on a multilingual store: they then show the built in text in each language. To change the wording of a theme text, use Edit default theme content in the theme's ... menu in your theme library. For a language Balm does not ship, Translate & Adapt can translate the theme texts too."},{"t":"Combined listings","p":"Features","u":"features.html#combined-listings","x":"Combined listings group separate products into one listing, for example one product per color, and are available to Shopify Plus stores through Shopify's Combined Listings app. Balm supports them with nothing to configure: On the product page, picking a value that belongs to another product of the listing switches the page to that product without a reload, keeping the values already chosen and updating the address. Swatches on product cards link to the matching product. In quick view, a value from another product loads that product into the modal. In the quick add option picker, such a value opens that product's page, where the full picker takes over."},{"t":"Pre-order","p":"Features","u":"features.html#pre-order","x":"Pre-order turns itself on: there is nothing to enable. A variant becomes a pre-order when its quantity is tracked, its stock is at 0 and Continue selling when out of stock is checked in the product admin. The add to cart button, the sticky add to cart bar and the quick add button then read Pre-order , or the Button label you set in Theme settings, Pre-order . The variant can still be bought, so the accelerated checkout buttons (Buy it now) stay visible, unlike on a sold out variant. The Stock status block keeps its own text. The label does not change how checkout works: the order is paid at checkout like any other. To take a deposit or charge later, use a pre-order app that creates selling plans; its options then show in the Purchase options block. Tell buyers when the product will ship, for example in a Text block or a Collapsible row."},{"t":"Type sizes","p":"Features","u":"features.html#type-sizes","x":"Every text of Balm sits on one fluid type scale, from phones to large screens. A size is reached at 390 px wide for its mobile value and at 1440 px for its desktop value, and grows in a straight line in between, so a heading never jumps from one size to another as the window widens. The text size settings of the sections and blocks follow the same rule, and their defaults sit on the scale: a section you add matches its neighbors without any tuning. To make the whole store read larger or smaller, move Heading scale or Body scale in Theme settings, Typography (80 to 130%). They multiply every size, those set in sections included, so the proportions between levels stay. To change one element, use its own size settings: they stay on the fluid rule and the scales still apply to them. Product card titles and prices are set once for all the grids in Theme settings, Product cards . The announcement bar and the mega menu switch their sizes at 1200 px, the menu breakpoint. Logos and decorative texts are sized on their own, off the scale: the Large logo of the footer fills its width, and the text behind cutouts of the product page or the two words across the Gallery banner keep a desktop and "},{"t":"Page width","p":"Features","u":"features.html#page-width","x":"One setting, Page width in Theme settings, Layout , sets how wide the shopping pages grow: the product page, the collection and search pages, and the Featured collection, Product recommendations and Recently viewed sections. Standard keeps them to 1400 px, Wide to 1600 px, and Full width with margins fills the screen less the side margins of the header, so the page, the breadcrumbs and the footer line up with the header's logo and icons. On a large screen, Wide shows bigger product cards and a bigger gallery; the card images are served at the new size, so they stay sharp. The other sections set their width with Section width ."},{"t":"Automatic header colors","p":"Features","u":"features.html#header-colors","x":"The header can lie over the top of the page, transparent, and wear the colors that read on what is under it, with nothing to set in each section. It does so with Header behavior on Transparent at top (the default: over the first section, then the card on scroll) or Adaptive (at every scroll position, on every page). In the Header section, set Colors over dark backgrounds to a color scheme with light text. Scheme 2 of the Balm preset, white on near black, is the default. Upload a light version of your logo in Logo for dark backgrounds . It shares the size and the place of the main logo, so nothing moves when they swap. Let the first section of the page reach under the header: Allow transparent header on a Hero, Slideshow, Video, Products showcase or Brand story hero, or Header over this section on the other sections that offer it (see The header over a section ). The header then reads the backgrounds painted under its middle line: colors, gradients, each product's gradient, and, over a picture or a video, a small thumbnail of the part it covers, overlay included. Over a dark background it takes the colors over dark backgrounds and the logo for dark backgrounds; over a light one, its"},{"t":"Section width","p":"Features","u":"features.html#section-width","x":"Almost every section has a Section width setting, right after its color scheme, with three options: Full width : the background, the picture or the video runs from one edge of the screen to the other. Text keeps a readable width inside. Full width with margins : the section stops at the side margins of the header. Its edges line up with the header's at every screen width, and, with Floating header (detached) on, with the edges of the floating header card. Page width : the section stops at the Page width of Theme settings, Layout, with its side margin, in line with the product, collection and search pages. Mixing the options on one page builds a rhythm: a Full width hero, products and texts at Page width, then a picture in Full width with margins whose rounded corners line up with a floating header. See Sections, Section width ."},{"t":"Glass","p":"Features","u":"features.html#glass","x":"Glass is the frosted look of Balm: a tinted, translucent fill with a fine border, which blurs what passes behind it. Two recipes in Theme settings, Glass effect drive every glass surface of the store, so one change restyles them all. Glass effect (Tint, Fill opacity, Blur, Border opacity) covers the large surfaces: the header card and its mega menu panels, the announcement bar in Glass style, the cart drawer, the filter drawer, quick view, the popups and the glass buttons. Glass elements (Element fill opacity, Element blur, Element border opacity) covers the small pieces inside sections: cards, FAQ questions, form fields, and the controls that sit over a picture, such as the carousel arrows, the Lookbook hotspots ( Hotspot colors set to Glass), the media controls of the product gallery and the Hero video controls. Pick Glass in the style setting of each element: Card style, Question style, Arrow style, Button style and so on. Glass labels measure their contrast and turn black or white when the text color would not read on the frost. Glass on phones can swap the blur for a near opaque fill on screens under 768 px, and visitors who ask for reduced transparency, or whose browser canno"},{"t":"Social media","p":"Features","u":"features.html#social-media","x":"Your social media profiles are typed once, in Theme settings, Social media , and every icon of the store reads them. In Theme settings, Social media, paste the full address of each profile you have, for example https://www.tiktok.com/@yourbrand . Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, X, YouTube, Pinterest, Snapchat, Threads, Tumblr, Vimeo and LinkedIn are offered. Choose where the icons appear: the Social media links block of the footer, the Social media links section, and the header on desktop with Show social media icons in the Header section. Only the networks with an address show, each with its icon, in a new tab. Screen readers name each link after your store, such as Balm on Instagram . The footer block can also show Shopify's Follow on Shop button. How your pages look when someone shares them is set separately, in Social media sharing ."},{"t":"Sticky add to cart","p":"Features","u":"features.html#sticky-add-to-cart","x":"A bar that keeps the product and its add to cart button within reach while the shopper scrolls a long product page. It is the Sticky add to cart section, which the product template places below the Product section. Enable the bar turns it on. Position (desktop) and Position (mobile) put it at the top or at the bottom of the screen; the bottom suits phones, where the main button quickly scrolls away. It shows the Product thumbnail (desktop and mobile apart), the Product title , the Selected variant (left out on a product without variants) and the Price , each one optional. By default it appears once the main buy button scrolls out of view; Always visible keeps it on screen. The button follows the variant chosen on the page and says Pre-order on a pre-order variant. Its colors are Button background and Button text ; with the Product gradient background, the product's end color becomes its accent when it stays readable. The back to top button lifts above the bar. In the theme editor, the bar steps aside while another section is selected."},{"t":"Spinning badge of a spotlight","p":"Features","u":"features.html#spotlight-spinning-badge","x":"Each Spotlight of the Products showcase can turn a round badge on its slide, set in the Spinning badge group of the spotlight. Unlike the Spinning badge block of the product page, which reads the product's custom.badge_label metafield, the spotlight's badge carries its own image or text. Type : None, Image (your own artwork) or Text. An Image spotlight with no picture shows the Spinning badge image of the section, shared by every spotlight. Text : written around a Shape , a circle or a rounded square. With Repeat text on, the text and its Separator repeat to fill the ring; off, the text is written once, centered on the Start angle (0 at the top, 90 on the right). Text size, weight, case and letter spacing per device, and a Center content : an image or an icon in the middle of the ring. Place : size and horizontal and vertical position on desktop and on mobile, in percent of the slide, Place behind the product , opacity, a link, and Show on mobile . Motion : Rotate , the time of One full turn and the Direction . The rotation stops for visitors who ask for reduced motion."},{"t":"Column selector","p":"Features","u":"features.html#collection-columns","x":"The Collection section can let shoppers choose how many products they see per row. Columns (desktop) and Columns (mobile) set the starting layout; then: Let visitors change the column count (desktop) adds 2, 3 and 4 buttons beside the sort. Let visitors change the column count (mobile) adds 1 and 2 buttons beside the filters on phones. On desktop the buttons sit on one row with the filters, the product count and the sort; on a phone, on one row with the Filter and sort button and the count. Each device keeps its own choice for the rest of the visit, after a filter or a page reload too. Both are off by default."},{"t":"Metafields","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html","x":"Metafields let one template give every product its own colors, texts and images. This page lists the metafields Balm reads, with the exact name, key and type to create."},{"t":"Before you start","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#before-you-start","x":"The theme cannot create a metafield definition; only you can, in your admin. This is a platform rule: a setting can only be connected to a definition that already exists, with the right type. So the definition always comes first, the connection second, the values third. Definitions are created in Settings, Custom data , under Products , Collections , Pages or Shop , depending on what carries the value. Type the Name exactly as listed below. The admin derives the key from the name, in lowercase with underscores, so the key matches on its own. If you rename a definition, check its key before saving: the connection works by key. Names are shown in quotation marks here and in the theme editor so you can see where they start and end. The quotation marks are not part of the name. The namespace and key are suggestions; the type is not. A setting refuses a definition of the wrong type. Every connectable setting repeats the definition it expects in its own help text in the editor."},{"t":"Metafields the theme reads directly","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#read-directly","x":"These keys need a definition and a value, and nothing else: the theme reads them by key, so there is nothing to connect in the theme editor. Create each definition once, with exactly this namespace and key, then fill the value on each product, in the Metafields card of the product page in your admin. Compare products reads no fixed key: each of its rows reads the metafield you name. See Compare products rows ."},{"t":"Badge label, step by step","p":"Metafields / Metafields the theme reads directly","u":"metafields.html#badge-label","x":"In your admin, open Settings , then Custom data , then Products . Choose Add definition . Name: Badge label . Check that the namespace and key read custom.badge_label . Select the type Single line text (under Text), keep One value , and save. Open a product, find the Metafields card, type the badge text in Badge label , for example Limited edition , and save. The badge now shows wherever that product appears as a card, in quick view and in Compare products. On the product page it shows when Badges on media is on Automatic or a Badge block is in the column. Its colors are in Theme settings, Product badges , unless the product has its own (below). Clear the value and the badge goes."},{"t":"Badge colors, step by step","p":"Metafields / Metafields the theme reads directly","u":"metafields.html#badge-colors","x":"Optional: only for products whose Custom badge should not wear the colors of Theme settings. In Settings, Custom data, Products , choose Add definition . Name: Badge color , namespace and key custom.badge_color , type Color . Save. Choose Add definition again. Name: Badge text color , namespace and key custom.badge_text_color , type Color . Save. Open a product that has a Badge label , and in its Metafields card pick a Badge color , for example a deep green. Pick a Badge text color too, or leave it empty. With only the badge color, the text is picked for you: the text color or the background color of Scheme 1, whichever contrasts more with the badge, or pure black or white when neither reaches 4.5:1. With only the text color, the text sits on the Custom background of Theme settings. Create both as Color : a value that is not a color, such as a word typed in a text metafield, is ignored. The two colors apply to the Custom badge only, never to Sale, Sold out or New, and not to the Spinning badge, which keeps the colors set in its block."},{"t":"Primary collection, step by step","p":"Metafields / Metafields the theme reads directly","u":"metafields.html#primary-collection","x":"Optional: for products that sit in several collections, to choose the one the breadcrumb trail shows. In Settings, Custom data, Products , choose Add definition . Name: Primary collection , namespace and key custom.primary_collection , type Collection (under References), one value. Save. Open a product, and in its Metafields card pick the collection in Primary collection . Check that Show breadcrumbs and Show the collection are on in Theme settings, Breadcrumbs . A visitor who arrives from a collection grid still sees that collection in the trail; the metafield decides for the others, such as a visitor coming from a search engine. Search engines read the same trail."},{"t":"Banner image, step by step","p":"Metafields / Metafields the theme reads directly","u":"metafields.html#banner-image","x":"Optional: for collections whose banner needs another picture than the collection image, or a precise framing. In Settings, Custom data, Collections , choose Add definition . Name: Banner image , namespace and key custom.banner_image , type File , with images accepted. Save. Open a collection in Products, Collections , and in its Metafields card pick the picture. To control the framing, set the focal point of the picture in Content, Files . The banner takes, in this order, this metafield, the Banner image of the Collection section, then the collection's own image. Shopify keeps no focal point on a collection's own image, which is why the metafield and the section setting exist."},{"t":"Page image, step by step","p":"Metafields / Metafields the theme reads directly","u":"metafields.html#page-image","x":"Optional: for pages linked from the main menu, so their link shows a picture in the dropdowns and in Image cards. In Settings, Custom data, Pages , choose Add definition . Name: Image , namespace and key custom.image , type File , with images accepted. Save. Open a page in Online Store, Pages , and pick its picture in the Metafields card. A page without it shows its link without a picture, and an Image cards block set to Automatic leaves it out."},{"t":"Tagline, step by step","p":"Metafields / Metafields the theme reads directly","u":"metafields.html#tagline","x":"In Settings, Custom data, Products , choose Add definition . Name: Tagline , namespace and key custom.tagline , type Single line text . Save. Fill it on each product, for example Rich overnight repair for dry skin . The default product template already has a Text block with Source set to Tagline under the title. On another template, add a Text block and choose that source. A product without a tagline shows nothing there, not even the space of the line. In the theme editor, a dimmed example stands in so you can place and size the block."},{"t":"Products showcase and Featured set, step by step","p":"Metafields / Metafields the theme reads directly","u":"metafields.html#showcase","x":"In Settings, Custom data, Products , create the definitions you want: Tagline ( custom.tagline , Single line text ), Background color ( custom.background_color , Color ) and Background color end ( custom.background_color_end , Color ). Fill them on each product, for example a soft sage and a deeper sage for a calming balm. In the theme editor, open a Spotlight block of the Products showcase, or the Featured set section, and pick the product in Product . There is nothing to connect: the name, the link, the tagline, the colors and the image follow. Keep the fields of the Override (optional) group empty: a filled field wins over the product. A spotlight set up before these settings existed keeps what was typed in it (name, tagline, colors, image, link) as overrides; clear those fields to let the product take over. A product without these values falls back cleanly: no tagline line, and the background of the section's color scheme. A spotlight with a background color and no end color is one color. In the theme editor a dimmed example stands in for a missing tagline. The product page reads the same definitions. In the Product section, set Background mode to Product gradient (metafields) "},{"t":"Per product background colors, step by step","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#per-product-background","x":"The most common use: one product template, a different background shade on every product. For a gradient, the quickest way needs no connection: create custom.background_color and custom.background_color_end , fill them, and set Background mode to Product gradient (metafields) (see Product gradient ). The steps below connect a metafield to the other modes: Solid color, Gradient (two colors) or Radial halo."},{"t":"Step 1. Create the definition (once)","p":"Metafields / Per product background colors, step by step","u":"metafields.html#step-1","x":"In your admin, open Settings, Custom data, Products and choose Add definition . Name: Background color . Namespace and key: custom.background_color . Type: Color . Save."},{"t":"Step 2. Connect it to the setting (once)","p":"Metafields / Per product background colors, step by step","u":"metafields.html#step-2","x":"In the theme editor, open a product page and select the Product section. Set Background mode to Solid color (or Gradient (two colors), or Radial halo; the same idea applies to each of their colors). Next to Background color , select the dynamic source icon (a small database symbol) and pick Background color . The field now shows the metafield name instead of a swatch. Save."},{"t":"Step 3. Fill in the values (per product)","p":"Metafields / Per product background colors, step by step","u":"metafields.html#step-3","x":"In your admin, open a product and scroll to the Metafields card. Set Background color to that product's shade and save. Products you leave empty fall back cleanly, as explained below."},{"t":"Step 4. Check it","p":"Metafields / Per product background colors, step by step","u":"metafields.html#step-4","x":"Open two products on the storefront, one with a value and one without. The first shows its own shade, the second falls back. If both look the same, the connection of step 2 was not saved. For a gradient, repeat step 1 with Background color end ( custom.background_color_end ) and connect it to Gradient end . For a halo, create Accent color ( custom.accent_color ) and connect it to Halo color ."},{"t":"Product metafields you connect","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#product-metafields","x":"Create these in Settings, Custom data, Products , then connect them with the dynamic source icon next to the setting. The names and keys are suggestions; only the type matters."},{"t":"Icon metafields, step by step","p":"Metafields / Product metafields you connect","u":"metafields.html#icon-metafields","x":"The Icon list of the product page holds up to three claims, each an Icon item block, and each claim can come from the product: an icon picture and a line of text per item, numbered by item. Create the ones you need: In Settings, Custom data, Products , add the definitions: for example Icon image 1 , type File , and Icon text 1 , type Multi-line text (or Single line text for one line). Fill them on each product, for example a leaf picture and Vegan formula . In the theme editor, open a product, select the first Icon item of the Icon list, then next to Icon image select the dynamic source icon and pick Icon image 1 . Do the same next to Heading with Icon text 1 . Repeat for the second and third items. These names and keys are suggestions: any key works, as long as the type matches, since you connect them yourself. An item whose heading and text both come back empty stays hidden on the storefront and leaves no gap; in the theme editor it keeps a small badge that says why."},{"t":"Metafields you type by key","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#typed-keys","x":"A few settings are plain text fields where you type the namespace.key yourself instead of using the dynamic source icon."},{"t":"Product list metafields","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#product-lists","x":"The Products setting of the Product upsell block, of the Complementary products block and of the cart drawer suggestions can be connected to a product metafield of type Product , set to accept a list of products. Each product then carries its own hand picked selection, for example Upsell products with the key custom.upsell_products . The block's Products come from setting must be on A manual selection ."},{"t":"Shop metafields","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#shop-metafields","x":"Every other section that paints a background (rich text, featured collection, FAQ, contact, image with text and so on) offers the same Section background settings. Those sections are not tied to a product, so their colors connect to shop metafields, created in Settings, Custom data, Shop . One value then applies storewide, which lets you restyle every connected section at once."},{"t":"Review metafields","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#reviews","x":"The Rating block, the ratings on product cards, in quick view and in Compare products read Shopify's standard review metafields, reviews.rating (Rating) and reviews.rating_count (Integer). Review apps fill them; you have nothing to create. Until they are filled, the ratings stay hidden."},{"t":"Compare products rows","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#compare","x":"Compare products has no metafield of its own. Each Row block with Source set to Metafield reads the product metafield you name in its Metafield setting, on every compared product, so you decide which facts the table compares. Type the metafield's name, exactly as it shows in Settings, Custom data, Products ( Skin type ), or its key ( custom.skin_type ). A name is turned into the key the admin gives it by default: namespace custom , the name in lowercase with underscores. If you changed the key of a definition, type the key. The field takes no dynamic source on purpose: a connected metafield would give the value of the page's product in every column. To name the row after the metafield, connect it to the row's Label instead, or leave Label empty to show the name you typed. For example, to compare three creams of a range: Create one definition per fact, as in the table. These names and keys are examples: any name works, as long as the row names the same metafield. Fill the values on each product you compare, in the Metafields card of the product. In the theme editor, open the Compare products section and add one Row block per fact. Keep Source on Metafield, type the name or the key i"},{"t":"What happens on a product with no value","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#empty-values","x":"Nothing breaks and nothing goes blank, which is what lets you fill only the products you care about. A background color that comes back empty falls through, in this order: the Fallback background color setting, if you set one; otherwise the background of the section's color scheme. In a Products showcase spotlight and in Featured set, the order is the override field, then the product's metafield, then the background of the section's color scheme. In the Product gradient mode of the product page, one color alone paints a flat background and no color leaves the color scheme; the fallback color is not used there. For the Custom badge, an empty custom.badge_color or custom.badge_text_color leaves the Custom colors of Theme settings. Behind cutout images, an empty tagline shows no text, and an empty custom.background_color_end gives the text the scheme text color. Never connect the fallback color itself to a metafield: it is the safety net. If one end of a gradient is empty, the other end fills the whole wash; if a halo color is empty, the halo is not drawn and the base color stays. An empty text, rich text or image metafield shows nothing on the storefront: never an example text, never"},{"t":"Settings that cannot be connected","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#not-connectable","x":"Shopify only allows connections on colors, text, rich text, images, videos, links, pages, collections, products and metaobjects. Sliders, checkboxes, dropdowns, the color scheme and Liquid code are fixed for the whole template. When one product needs a different value for one of those, give it a second product template ."},{"t":"Custom code","p":"Custom code","u":"custom-code.html","x":"Balm is built to be shaped from the theme editor, without code. If you or a developer do edit the theme code, read this page first."},{"t":"Get help from a Shopify Partner","p":"Custom code","u":"custom-code.html#hire-a-partner","x":"Code customizations are outside the scope of Balm support. For custom features, design changes or integrations, we recommend working with a Shopify Partner: developers and agencies vetted by Shopify, listed in the Shopify Partner Directory ."},{"t":"Try the editor first","p":"Custom code","u":"custom-code.html#before-coding","x":"Many changes need no edit to the theme files: The Custom Liquid section, and the Liquid blocks of the product page and of the content sections, accept your own Liquid, HTML and app snippets. Shopify's Custom CSS field, at the bottom of each section's settings and in Theme settings, takes CSS scoped to that section or to the whole store. The Apps section and app blocks place app content without touching the code. Code added this way is kept when you update the theme."},{"t":"Theme updates and your code","p":"Custom code","u":"custom-code.html#updates-and-code","x":"When you update Balm, Shopify installs the new version as a separate copy and carries over your theme editor settings and content, but not the changes you made in the theme files. Keep a list of every file you changed and why, so the changes can be applied again to the new version."},{"t":"What support covers","p":"Custom code","u":"custom-code.html#support-scope","x":"Balm support covers the theme as shipped. When a problem shows up on a theme whose code was modified, we may ask you to reproduce it on an unmodified copy of Balm first. See Support ."},{"t":"FAQ","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html","x":"Answers to the questions merchants ask most about Balm."},{"t":"Can I use Balm on more than one store?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#can-i-use-balm-on-more-than-one-store","x":"A theme bought from the Shopify Theme Store is licensed for one store. To use Balm on another store, buy it again from that store. Trying the theme is free on any store."},{"t":"How do I update Balm without losing my settings?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-update-balm-without-losing-my-settings","x":"When an update is available, your theme library shows a notice. Shopify adds the new version as a separate copy that keeps your theme editor settings and content. Preview it, then publish it. Changes you made in the theme code are not carried over; see Custom code ."},{"t":"How do I make the header transparent over my hero?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-make-the-header-transparent-over-my-hero","x":"In the Header section, keep Header behavior on Transparent at top , the default, or choose Adaptive . Make sure the first section of the page is a Hero, Slideshow, Video, Products showcase or Brand story hero with Allow transparent header checked, or another section with Header over this section checked. If your hero is dark, upload a light version of your logo in Logo for dark backgrounds , and check that Colors over dark backgrounds is a scheme with light text. The header picks them on its own over a dark image. A floating announcement bar over the same image can follow those colors: check Use the header's colors over dark backgrounds in the Announcement bar section. See the white header example . On the product page, the Product section can run its Product gradient under the transparent header: see Extend the gradient under the header ."},{"t":"Why does the product gradient not reach under the header?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-does-the-product-gradient-not-reach-under-the-header","x":"Four conditions, all needed: Background mode of the Product section is Product gradient (metafields) , Extend the background under the header is checked, the Header section has Header behavior on Transparent at top or Adaptive, and the Product section is the first section of the product template. A Solid announcement bar in full width stays above the gradient; a Floating or Glass bar lets it run underneath. The header picks light or dark colors for each product on its own: if its text is hard to read over a dark gradient, check that Colors over dark backgrounds in the Header is a scheme with light text. See Extend the gradient under the header ."},{"t":"Why is there no country or language selector in my header?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-is-there-no-country-or-language-selector-in-my-header","x":"The selectors only show when there is a choice to make. The country selector needs at least two countries or regions in Settings, Markets ; the language selector needs at least two published languages in Settings, Languages , active in the visitor's market. Then check that Country and language selectors in the Header section is not set to Off. See Country and language selectors ."},{"t":"Why are there no filters on my collection pages?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-are-there-no-filters-on-my-collection-pages","x":"Filters come from Shopify's free Search & Discovery app. Install it, add the filters you want (availability, price, product type, color and so on), then check that Enable filters is on in the Collection and Search sections. A filter only shows when the products of the page have values for it."},{"t":"How do I set up a mega menu?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-set-up-a-mega-menu","x":"Create your main menu in your admin first. Then, in the Header section, add a Mega menu block and type the exact title of a top level menu item in Linked menu item , for example Shop . Pick a Layout : Links and images builds the panel from that item's sub-links on its own; Custom blocks uses the Link column, Image, Image cards, Products, Promo or Banner blocks you add inside it. The panel opens when a shopper hovers that item. See Mega menu blocks ."},{"t":"How do I give each product its own background color?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-give-each-product-its-own-background-color","x":"Create two product metafield definitions of type Color, Background color ( custom.background_color ) and Background color end ( custom.background_color_end ), and fill them on each product. Then set Background mode of the Product section to Product gradient (metafields) : there is nothing to connect, and one color alone gives a flat background. For a solid color or a radial halo, connect the metafield to the setting instead. Both ways are on Metafields ."},{"t":"How do I make all headings, or all text, larger?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-make-all-headings-or-all-text-larger","x":"Use Heading scale and Body scale in Theme settings, Typography. They multiply every size of the theme, the ones set in sections and blocks included, from 80 to 130%. Changing each section's sizes one by one is only worth it for a single element. See Type sizes ."},{"t":"Why is there no text behind my product image?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-is-there-no-text-behind-my-product-image","x":"The text of Text behind cutouts only shows behind PNG and WebP images; JPG images, videos and 3D models never get it. Check that Show on desktop or Show on mobile is on for the device you are looking at, and that the first media of the gallery is a PNG or WebP image when Apply to is First image only. With Text on Product tagline, a product whose custom.tagline is empty shows no text. See Text behind cutout images ."},{"t":"Why does the spinning badge not show on some products?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-does-the-spinning-badge-not-show-on-some-products","x":"The ring prints the product's custom.badge_label metafield and has no text of its own: a product with no value shows no ring. Fill the metafield on that product (see Badge label, step by step ). With Next to the title , the page also needs a Title block."},{"t":"Where are Balm spotlight, Lifestyle strip, the Sticky add to cart and Quantity blocks?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#where-are-balm-spotlight-lifestyle-strip-the-sticky-add-to-c","x":"They belonged to preview versions of Balm and were removed before release, together with the free text of the spinning badge. Balm spotlight , the second version of the Product section: its gradient and its spinning badge are now the Product gradient background mode and the positions of the Spinning badge block, on the one Product section. Lifestyle strip , two photos side by side: the section has been removed. Sticky add to cart block : the bar is the Sticky add to cart section, placed below the Product section in the product template. Spinning badge text : the ring of the product page reads the product's custom.badge_label metafield only. The spotlights of the Products showcase keep a text of their own: see Spinning badge of a spotlight . Quantity block : the quantity selector is part of the Buy buttons block, set by Quantity selector (desktop) and Quantity selector (mobile) ."},{"t":"Why can I not connect a setting to my metafield?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-can-i-not-connect-a-setting-to-my-metafield","x":"Three usual causes. The definition does not exist yet: create it in Settings, Custom data first. The type does not match: a color setting only accepts a Color metafield, an image setting a File metafield. Or the definition was created for the wrong resource: product page settings need a Products definition, other sections a Shop definition. The help text of each connectable setting names the exact definition it expects."},{"t":"How do I add product reviews and star ratings?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-add-product-reviews-and-star-ratings","x":"Install a reviews app that writes Shopify's standard review metafields (most do). Balm's Rating block, the ratings on product cards and quick view read them automatically once reviews come in. If the app offers an app block for its review list, add it to the product page from the block picker."},{"t":"How do I add a size guide or ingredients list to product pages?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-add-a-size-guide-or-ingredients-list-to-product-pag","x":"Create a page with the content in Online Store, Pages. On the product page, add a Popup block (a link that opens a dialog) or a Collapsible row , and set Content comes from to A page . For content that differs per product, connect the block's Content to a rich text metafield instead."},{"t":"Can I change the color of the Shop Pay or PayPal buttons?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#can-i-change-the-color-of-the-shop-pay-or-paypal-buttons","x":"No theme can. The accelerated checkout buttons are drawn by Shopify with the brand colors of each payment provider. Balm matches everything Shopify allows: height, corner radius, spacing and the loading placeholder. See The accelerated checkout buttons ."},{"t":"How do I show a free shipping progress bar?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-show-a-free-shipping-progress-bar","x":"In Theme settings, Cart , keep Show the free shipping bar checked and type the amount in Free shipping threshold . The bar only displays progress: create the matching free shipping rate or automatic discount in your admin, and keep the two amounts the same, or buyers will be promised something checkout does not apply."},{"t":"Why does the Buy it now button disappear on some variants?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-does-the-buy-it-now-button-disappear-on-some-variants","x":"The accelerated checkout buttons (Buy it now, Shop Pay, PayPal and the other wallets) are hidden while the selected variant is sold out, since it cannot be bought, and come back when the shopper picks a variant in stock. A variant that sells as a pre-order can be bought, so it keeps them. See The accelerated checkout buttons ."},{"t":"How do I offer pre-orders?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-offer-pre-orders","x":"Set the variant to continue selling when out of stock in the product admin. At 0 stock its buttons read Pre-order, or the label you set in Theme settings, Pre-order. To take a deposit or charge later, use a pre-order app. See Pre-order ."},{"t":"How do I translate my store?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-translate-my-store","x":"Add and publish your languages in Settings, Languages. Balm's own texts are already translated into French, German, Italian and Spanish. Translate what you typed in the editor with the Translate & Adapt app. See Translations ."},{"t":"The newsletter popup does not appear. What should I check?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#the-newsletter-popup-does-not-appear-what-should-i-check","x":"Enable popup is checked in the Newsletter popup section, and the section is on the template you are viewing (by default, the home page only). You closed it earlier: it stays hidden for the number of days in Reappear after . Test in a private window. The Open delay has not passed yet."},{"t":"Why does my header change color as I scroll?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-does-my-header-change-color-as-i-scroll","x":"With Header behavior on Transparent at top or Adaptive, the header reads what lies under it and wears the colors that read best there: its own color scheme and logo over a light background, Colors over dark backgrounds and Logo for dark backgrounds over a dark one. With Adaptive it does so at every scroll position, so it changes as dark and light sections pass under it. To keep one look everywhere, set Header behavior to Standard . See Automatic header colors ."},{"t":"How do I line up a section with the header or make it edge to edge?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-line-up-a-section-with-the-header-or-make-it-edge-t","x":"Use the section's Section width setting. Full width runs the background or the picture from one edge of the screen to the other, Full width with margins stops at the side margins of the header, so the section lines up with a floating header card, and Page width lines it up with the product and collection pages. See Section width ."},{"t":"Where do I add my Instagram, TikTok and other social media links?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#where-do-i-add-my-instagram-tiktok-and-other-social-media-li","x":"In Theme settings, Social media : paste the full address of each profile. The icons then show in the footer's Social media links block and in the Social media links section, and in the header on desktop when Show social media icons is checked. Networks without an address stay hidden. See Social media ."},{"t":"How do I hide the Sale badges in one section only?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-hide-the-sale-badges-in-one-section-only","x":"Set that section's Badges setting to Custom only (only your custom.badge_label badges) or None . The other sections keep their own choice. Every section with product cards has it, as do the Bento Product tile and the Complementary products block. See Choose the badges of each section ."},{"t":"How do I let shoppers choose the number of columns on collection pages?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-let-shoppers-choose-the-number-of-columns-on-collec","x":"In the Collection section, check Let visitors change the column count (desktop) , which adds 2, 3 and 4 buttons beside the sort, and Let visitors change the column count (mobile) , which adds 1 and 2 buttons beside the filters on phones. Each device keeps the shopper's choice for the rest of the visit. See Column selector ."},{"t":"My speed score dropped after I turned on the page loader. Why?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#my-speed-score-dropped-after-i-turned-on-the-page-loader-why","x":"A loader covers the page while it loads, which speed tools measure as a slower page. Set Page loader to First visit only , the recommended setting, or turn it off. Every page shows it on each page view and has the largest effect."},{"t":"Changelog","p":"Changelog","u":"changelog.html","x":"What changed in each version of Balm. The version installed in your store is shown in your theme library, under the theme name."},{"t":"1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","p":"Changelog","u":"changelog.html#v-1-0-0-2026-10-13","x":"Initial release."},{"t":"Preset (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-preset","x":"Balm: clean and neutral. A white scheme, a near black scheme and two violet schemes, Outfit for headings (400) and Inter for body text, sentence case headings and buttons, small buttons, softly rounded corners (12 px buttons, 20 px cards), a white frosted glass and pages in Full width with margins. The preset carries four color schemes, a font pairing, corner radii, a glass recipe and typography recipes. Every text measures a contrast of at least 4.5:1. The templates and the header and footer groups follow the demo store's layout: the same sections, in the same order, with the same style settings, and no image, product, collection or metafield of the demo. Sections and blocks added in the theme editor come with example texts that say how to use them, in the language of the theme editor (English, French, German, Italian or Spanish): they are the default values of their settings, which Shopify translates."},{"t":"Theme settings (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-theme-settings","x":"Color schemes with seven roles: background, optional background gradient, text, button, button label, secondary background and accent. Heading and body fonts from the Shopify font library, and three shared typography recipes: headings (case, style, weight), button labels (case, letter spacing, style), labels and small text (case). Type sizes: one fluid type scale for the whole theme, from 390 px to 1440 px wide (product title 32 to 44 px, section headings 26 to 36, card titles 15 to 17, card prices 14 to 16, body text 15 to 16, small text 12 to 13, footer column titles 13 to 14), with line height and letter spacing per level. Every size setting of the sections and blocks is fluid too, its mobile value at 390 px and its desktop value at 1440 px, and its default sits on the scale. The announcement bar and the mega menu keep their switch at the menu breakpoint. Heading scale and Body scale (80 to 130 %) multiply every heading size and every body size, section settings included. Corner style: four maximum radii, for buttons, cards, form fields and media. Buttons, for every button of the theme, primary and secondary: Size (Small, Medium, Large) sets the height, padding and text size on "},{"t":"Header, footer and popups (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-header-footer-and-popups","x":"Header with a solid or glass card, a floating detached card, an image logo or a text wordmark, a logo for dark backgrounds, three level menus, a mobile menu as a sheet or a full height drawer, predictive search, Shopify customer accounts and a cart counter. Once the page scrolls, a sticky floating card blurs the page that passes under it across the whole width, its side margins included, and fades out just under the card. Header behavior, one setting: Standard (the card and its color scheme, always), Transparent at top (the default: transparent over a first section that allows it, in the colors that suit that section's tone, then the card on scroll) or Adaptive (transparent or glass at every scroll position, on every page, its colors and logo following the section under it). Colors over dark backgrounds (a color scheme with light text) and a logo for dark backgrounds; over light backgrounds the header keeps its own scheme and main logo. Background when scrolled (Glass or Transparent) in Adaptive only. The tone needs no setting in the sections: the header reads sixteen points on its middle line and the first background painted under each (a color, a gradient by its stops, a product "},{"t":"Home page and content sections (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-home-page-and-content-sections","x":"Hero with an image or a Shopify hosted video, separate desktop and mobile media cropped on their focal point, autoplay per device, a sound button, loop, stop or cover at the end, three controls styles that appear with the video, the cover sharp or blurred while the video loads, and content placement per device. An eyebrow above the heading and a subheading under it. The hero keeps its height when the phone's address bar shows or hides, so its content and button stay in place. Without an image or a video, its placeholder takes the color scheme's background and text, so the heading reads at once. Products showcase: full screen product spotlights with a scroll pinned wipe, a snap mode, and on phones either the same animation and scroll mode as desktop with a layout of their own, or stacked spotlights. Highlights with claims, a featured set cartouche and watermarks. Claim 1 to 4 text are rich text fields that take a metafield of the spotlight's product, of type Single line text or Multi-line text, each line on its own line. Icon and text gap (desktop, mobile) sets the space the eye sees between a claim's icon and the top of its capitals (8 and 4 px by default, 0 to touch); a picked ico"},{"t":"Product page (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-product-page","x":"One product template built from blocks: title, vendor, price, SKU, rating, text, variant picker (buttons, dropdown menu, color and image swatches, signature pill, packs menu), volume pricing, purchase options, gift card recipient, buy buttons with the quantity and its quantity rules, dynamic checkout (hidden while the selected variant is unavailable) and Shop Pay Installments, stock status, back in stock, pickup availability, payment icons, product upsell, complementary products, description, collapsible rows, popup, specifications, icon list, image, badge, spinning badge, share, product navigation and Liquid. App blocks drop into the same column. Five buy button styles (Solid, Outline, Soft, Signature pill, Glass), and a packs menu that welds to the signature pill. Section background per product through metafields, with a fallback color and the color scheme as safety net, plus a background illustration (a decorative image behind the product area, under the media and the product information, one per product through a File metafield, the product's first image when left empty; by default on the media side, left on desktop and at the top on mobile, 55 percent of the section wide on de"},{"t":"Product cards and quick add (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-product-cards-and-quick-add","x":"Product cards with a second image on hover, the vendor, the rating, color swatches with a +N count, three card styles, the element order and the alignment, depending on the section. Quick add in one setting (Off, Single-variant products, All products) on the collection, search, featured collection, recently viewed, lookbook and compare products sections. Single-variant products add in one click, the others open an option picker in a modal, the cart drawer opens and the page never reloads. A value of a combined listing hands over to the sibling product page. Theme settings, Product cards, Quick add button: one style for the button of every card (Solid, Outline, Text link, Icon only with a bag icon), Auto or Full width, below the product details or on the image (shown on hover on desktop, always on touch screens), and the color scheme's button colors or custom background, text and border colors. The corners follow Theme settings, Corner style. The defaults keep the solid button under the details. Its Size follows Theme settings, Buttons, or sets Small, Medium or Large for the buttons of the cards alone. Theme settings, Product cards, Hover effect (Fade, Swap, Zoom). Fade crossfades t"},{"t":"Quick view (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-quick-view","x":"A Quick view setting (Off, Show on hover, Always show) on the collection, featured collection, search, recently viewed and lookbook sections opens a product in a modal without leaving the page: gallery with thumbnails, price with badges and unit price, rating, the product page's variant picker with swatches, quantity rules, purchase options, add to cart (the cart drawer opens), pickup availability, a short description and a link to the product page. Its gallery plays the product's rich media in their slides: Shopify hosted videos, YouTube and Vimeo videos (loaded when the visitor presses play) and 3D models; a video stops when its slide is left or the quick view closes. Theme settings, Quick view sets what the modal shows, the description source and length, the color scheme and the card material (Solid, Tinted glass, Glass), and can preload a product when the pointer rests on its card. Without JavaScript the trigger opens the product page. Theme settings, Quick view, Button on cards: icon (Eye, Plus, Expand, Bag), shape (Automatic, Circle, Rounded square, Pill with label), size on desktop and on mobile, and colors (color scheme, custom, or Glass from Theme settings, Glass effect). "},{"t":"Product badges (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-product-badges","x":"Sale, Sold out, New and Custom badges on the product cards, in quick view and in the compare products table, with their position (top left, top right), shape (button corners or pill) and colors in Theme settings. Every badge comes from the product. Sale shows only when the compare-at price is above the price, and reads Sale, the percentage off or the amount saved. Sold out follows the stock. New is off by default, and follows either a product tag (new by default) or the creation date within a number of days you set. Custom reads the custom.badge_label metafield directly, with nothing to connect in the editor. The Custom badge takes the product's own colors from two optional Color metafields, custom.badge_color (background) and custom.badge_text_color (text), everywhere it shows. Left empty, they use the Custom colors of Theme settings. With a background and no text color, the text turns dark or light, whichever contrasts more, always at least 4.5:1. On the product page, Badges on media (Off or Automatic) draws the same badges on the gallery, the Badge block draws them in the info column, and the spinning badge turns the custom.badge_label text. Sale and Sold out follow the selected"},{"t":"Pre-order (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-pre-order","x":"A variant that keeps selling at 0 stock shows Pre-order on the add to cart button, the sticky bar and the quick add button, with an optional custom label."},{"t":"Page loader (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-page-loader","x":"A page loader shown on the first visit only or on every page: logo only, logo with a progress bar, logo with a spinner, or progress bar only, on a solid or glass background with its own color scheme. Fade, Slide up, Split, Zoom or Circle reveal exits, optional page transitions, and minimum and maximum display times. The progress bar follows the page as it loads, with square or rounded ends, a thickness of 1 to 6 px and a None, Smooth or Shimmer animation. The loader sits above every other layer, and a preview mode shows it in the theme editor."},{"t":"Age verifier (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-age-verifier","x":"A modal that asks visitors to confirm their age, with the minimum age, texts and button labels, a message or a redirect on decline, a memory in days, an optional background image, a color scheme and three card materials. It waits for the page loader, never shows at checkout, and shows in the theme editor only with Preview checked."},{"t":"Back to top (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-back-to-top","x":"A round button in a bottom corner, shown after a set scroll distance, on desktop and mobile separately. It lifts above the sticky add to cart bar and steps aside from the hero video controls; the scroll is smooth, or instant when the visitor prefers reduced motion. Three styles: Solid (the button colors of the color scheme), Custom (a background color and an icon color) and Glass (the theme's glass recipe, with an outlined icon that reads over any content, and the near opaque fallback of the other glass surfaces)."},{"t":"Collection navigation (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-collection-navigation","x":"A menu of collection links shown as a row of pills above or below the collection banner, the current collection highlighted, scrolling sideways on mobile."},{"t":"Pagination (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-pagination","x":"Page numbers, a Load more button or infinite scroll on the collection and search pages. Load more and infinite scroll add the next page under the grid with a Showing X of Y counter; infinite scroll loads three pages on its own, then hands over to the button so the footer stays reachable."},{"t":"Promo tiles (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-promo-tiles","x":"Promo tile blocks, up to four, on the collection and featured collection grids: an image with a mobile version, a heading, text, a button and a link, a color scheme, a position in the grid and a width of one or two columns. They appear on the first page only, so Load more and infinite scroll never repeat them."},{"t":"Before and after (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-before-and-after","x":"Two images compared with a draggable handle, horizontal or vertical, with labels, a starting position, a round or line handle, contained, page or full width (Page width lines it up with the other sections, the page margins on each side), heading and text, and keyboard access through a slider."},{"t":"Recently viewed (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-recently-viewed","x":"The products a visitor opened, newest first, from a list kept in the visitor's own browser. The section takes no space until there is a history, can leave out the current product, and shows as a grid or a slider on mobile, with quick add and quick view."},{"t":"Lookbook and hotspots (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-lookbook-and-hotspots","x":"An image with product or text hotspots, positioned separately on desktop and mobile. On desktop a hotspot opens a popover with the product card and its quick add; on a phone it opens a sheet from the bottom of the screen. An Image with product list layout lines the products up beside the image, and a card and its hotspot light up together. Hotspot shape (Circle, Rounded, Square), Hotspot icon (Plus, Dot, None), Hotspot colors from the color scheme or Custom (Hotspot color, Hotspot icon color), Hotspot size on desktop and on mobile (24 px at least). In the theme editor a selected hotspot is ringed and its card stays closed, so the picture stays in sight while it is placed."},{"t":"Compare products (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-compare-products","x":"Up to five products side by side, with image, price, availability, vendor and rating rows, and Row blocks. A row's Label (a text, or a metafield through a dynamic source) sits in the left column; its value is read on every compared product from its Source: Metafield, Vendor, Product type, Tags, SKU, Barcode, Weight or Unit price. Metafield takes the metafield's name as in the admin (Skin type) or its key (custom.skin_type), in a field without dynamic source, so each column reads its own product. Every metafield type is drawn as such (yes and no as icons, a list in a sentence, a number with the row's Unit, rich text, several lines, money, rating, color, image, references by title), and in the theme editor a row whose metafield no compared product has says so. Differences can be highlighted, an empty value shows a hyphen that screen readers read as n/a, and on a phone the label column stays in place while the products scroll."},{"t":"Gift wrapping (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-gift-wrapping","x":"A checkbox in the cart drawer and on the cart page adds the wrapping product you pick in Theme settings, in quantity 1, and records the cart attribute Gift wrapping: Yes. An optional gift message, up to the length you set, is saved as the cart attribute Gift message. Both reach the order."},{"t":"Cart (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-cart","x":"Theme settings, Cart sets up the whole cart in one place. Cart type: a drawer, the cart page, or a notification that confirms each add with the line just added, View cart and Check out. The drawer and the cart page share the same lines, recommendations, order note, discount code, free shipping bar, totals and checkout, in the same style. The cart page shows the lines beside a summary that follows the scroll, and works without JavaScript. Style: Solid (the color scheme's background) or Glass (the global glass effect over the whole drawer, top to bottom). Floating detaches the drawer and the notification from the screen edges by margins set for desktop and mobile, their corners following Corner style; otherwise the drawer runs the full height against the edge. Text colors: the color scheme, or Auto, light or dark from the drawer's real background, glass included, at a contrast of at least 4.5:1. The chosen colors reach everything in the drawer: title, free shipping bar, lines, recommendations, totals, fields, icons, hairlines and buttons. Auto reads gradients and pictures behind the drawer, at each opening and again when the page behind changes (a new slide or spotlight, a scroll), w"},{"t":"Collection, search and other pages (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-collection-search-and-other-pages","x":"Collection and search pages with filters and sorting from Search & Discovery, in a column, a drawer or a horizontal bar, with value counts, a price slider, color swatches and a results count. Visitors can change the column count or switch to a list view: Let visitors change the column count (desktop) offers 2, 3 or 4 columns and (mobile) 1 or 2, each device keeping its own choice; the buttons sit in the toolbar, on one row with the filters button (or the bar's filters, at the left), the count and the sort on desktop, and on one row with the Filter and sort button and the count on a phone. The filter drawer (phones, and the Drawer layout) opens over the announcement bar and the header, full height, with its title and close button, the filters in accordions, Sort by on phones, and Clear all and Apply fixed at the bottom; the page stays still behind it, Tab stays inside and Escape closes it. Theme settings, Filters, Filter drawer style: Solid (the section's color scheme) or Glass (the global Glass effect, like the cart drawer). Page: Content width Page width (the default, the column of Theme settings, Layout, lined up with the header's content), Standard (a 760 px reading column, the "},{"t":"Translations (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-translations","x":"Storefront and theme editor in English, French, German, Italian and Spanish. Text settings for interface labels left empty show the translated default in every language."},{"t":"Empty content (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-empty-content","x":"A heading, text, answer, testimonial, announcement, highlight or product detail left empty shows nothing, not even its space, in the theme editor too: no example text stands in for it. In the theme editor an empty block keeps its frame so it can be selected, empty images keep their placeholder, and a section with nothing to show shows a neutral placeholder box instead of disappearing. Sections added from the theme editor come with values that explain how to use each setting, in every language of the editor."},{"t":"Accessibility (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-accessibility","x":"A skip link, landmarks and headings on every template, one h1 per template, visible focus rings and 24 px touch targets. Focus kept inside the popups, the drawers, quick view and the age verifier, and live regions for variant changes and for the products added by Load more. Carousels with tab semantics and pause controls, a pause button on the marquee, and a before and after handle usable from the keyboard. Reduced motion respected: no video autoplay, no turning badge, instant scrolling and a still loader. Glass button labels switch to black or white when their contrast would fall below the floor. Every image has an alt attribute: the image's alt text, or an empty one when it has none (decorative). Routine steps are a real list. The previous and next product links keep a contrast of at least 4.5:1. Shopify's cookie banner keeps the look set in the admin: the theme no longer restyles it. Theme editor labels use Shopify's vocabulary and American spelling: heading, carousel, color, center."},{"t":"Performance (1.0.0 (2026-10-13))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-13)","u":"changelog.html#v-performance","x":"Stylesheets scoped per section and block, subset by page, and feature scripts loaded only on the pages where the feature renders. The hero video loads after the load event and the browser's first idle moment, over its cover, which paints first. The product page background no longer moves the layout while the page loads (its aurora layer starts at the top of the section). Store links in scripts and fallbacks come from Shopify's routes, so a store with a language or a market in its URL (/fr) keeps it. In the first two places of a template, a background picture and its 32 px blurred rendition load first, with a high priority, so the flat color never shows; picture covers (hero, store locator, gallery banner, featured set, password, collection banner) load at once with their blurred rendition under them. One image per device on the slideshow, eager loading reserved for the first section, the hero video loaded after the page by default, and the animation library loaded on demand. Glass surfaces fall back to a near opaque fill under reduced transparency, and on phones when the merchant picks Near opaque."},{"t":"Support","p":"Support","u":"support.html","x":"Balm support answers questions about the theme and fixes its bugs. Here is what it covers and how to reach it."},{"t":"What support covers","p":"Support","u":"support.html#covered","x":"Bugs in the theme as shipped: something that does not work as this documentation describes. Questions about the theme: installing it, its settings, sections, blocks and features, and how to reach a result with them."},{"t":"What support does not cover","p":"Support","u":"support.html#not-covered","x":"Customizations : changes to the theme code, new features, custom designs, or code added in Custom Liquid sections, Liquid blocks or Custom CSS. For this work we recommend a Shopify Partner . Problems caused by edits to the theme files. We may ask you to reproduce the problem on an unmodified copy of Balm. Third party apps and services, and Shopify features outside the theme (checkout, payments, shipping rules, domains). For those, contact the app developer or Shopify Support."},{"t":"Response time","p":"Support","u":"support.html#response-time","x":"We reply within two business days (Monday to Friday), usually sooner."},{"t":"How to send a request","p":"Support","u":"support.html#request","x":"Use the support form . To help us answer in one go, include: your store address ( yourstore.myshopify.com ) and the name of the theme in your library; the link of the page where the problem happens; what you did, what you expected and what happened instead, with a screenshot or a short video if you can; the browser and device you used; whether the theme code was modified. Before writing, it is worth checking the FAQ and searching this documentation. If an app could be involved, try with it turned off."}];
